  ('ed23b9cf-8b68-5a38-acc9-797c33e61564', 'ea65b685-d0c0-5aa8-bb8d-d6bb01f68d36', 'What a library is', 'Complete the sentences.

A program library is a collection of pre-written and pre-[[1]] code. A programmer can [[2]] a library function from their own program instead of writing the code again. A library that is joined to the program only when the program runs is called a [[3]] library.', 'fill_blank', 3, 'easy', 'complete', 'AUTO', 11, '60897a48-c2f2-526e-b15e-c52852e09a07', '317d0f1c-ccad-563c-ae3a-ff3647e1d2d8', '{"blank_count":3}'::jsonb, 'original', null, true, 'published', null, null, 0),
