  ('0c445267-d164-5de6-98e8-65082e23b986', 'ea65b685-d0c0-5aa8-bb8d-d6bb01f68d36', 'Assembly language program', '**Assembly language mnemonics**

| Mnemonic | Description |
|---|---|
| INP | Retrieve user input and store it in the Accumulator. |
| OUT | Output the value stored in the Accumulator. |
| LDA | Load the Accumulator with the contents of the memory address given. |
| STA | Store the value in the Accumulator in the memory address given. |
| ADD | Add the contents of the memory address to the Accumulator. |
| SUB | Subtract the contents of the memory address from the Accumulator. |
| BRP | Branch/Jump to the address given if the Accumulator is zero or positive. |
| BRZ | Jump to the address given in case the Accumulator is zero. |
| BRA | Jump to the address given. |
| HLT | Stop the code. |
| DAT | Used to associate a label to a free memory address. An optional value can also be used to be stored at the memory address. |

Assembly language instructions are written as mnemonics.', 'structured', 8, 'exam', null, 'AI', 11, '90094a74-5e7b-589b-af06-e75a04fd67d7', 'e08575f5-7d57-59f0-ac37-8ef870267c04', '{}'::jsonb, 'past_paper', 'NIS 2026 Paper 3 Q1', false, 'published', null, null, 0),
  ('5acaff87-08e3-53d4-ba8f-ac4470278c5b', 'ea65b685-d0c0-5aa8-bb8d-d6bb01f68d36', 'Assembly language program (a)', 'Give **one** example of an assembly language instruction used for transferring data.', 'short_answer', 1, 'exam', 'state', 'AI', 11, '90094a74-5e7b-589b-af06-e75a04fd67d7', 'e08575f5-7d57-59f0-ac37-8ef870267c04', '{"answer_lines":1}'::jsonb, 'past_paper', 'NIS 2026 Paper 3 Q1(a)', false, 'published', '0c445267-d164-5de6-98e8-65082e23b986', '(a)', 0),
  ('cc87f994-e997-5915-af4e-32e2e037827a', 'ea65b685-d0c0-5aa8-bb8d-d6bb01f68d36', 'Assembly language program (b)(i)', 'Assembly language code is given below.

```assembly
Address  Label     Instruction
00       START     LDA COUNT
01                 ADD ONE
02                 STA COUNT
03                 INP
04                 STA INPUT
05                 BRP CHECKR
06                 BRA START
07       CHECKR    LDA INPUT
08                 SUB RANGE
09                 BRZ OK
10                 BRP START
11       OK        LDA INPUT
12                 ADD ONE
13                 OUT
14                 LDA COUNT
15                 OUT
16                 HLT
17       ONE       DAT 1
18       RANGE     DAT 10
19       INPUT     DAT
20       COUNT     DAT 0
```

