Write pseudocode or program code for calculating the total number of goals that are stored in the array goals.', 'code_completion', 3, 'exam', 'write', 'AI', 11, '90094a74-5e7b-589b-af06-e75a04fd67d7', '0710a64d-c26c-5ed3-9685-d0a60307d3c8', '{"language":"pseudocode","starter_code":""}'::jsonb, 'past_paper', 'NIS 2026 Paper 3 Q4(e)(i)', false, 'published', '0d2437b0-6e21-5508-ab55-593089d1fd26', '(e)(i)', 6),
  ('cde3c528-8d14-56af-be2c-6fcdb2ae3577', 'ea65b685-d0c0-5aa8-bb8d-d6bb01f68d36', 'Football player web page (e)(ii)', 'Write pseudocode or program code for calculating the average number of goals per match.', 'code_completion', 1, 'exam', 'write', 'AI', 11, '90094a74-5e7b-589b-af06-e75a04fd67d7', '0710a64d-c26c-5ed3-9685-d0a60307d3c8', '{"language":"pseudocode","starter_code":""}'::jsonb, 'past_paper', 'NIS 2026 Paper 3 Q4(e)(ii)', false, 'published', '0d2437b0-6e21-5508-ab55-593089d1fd26', '(e)(ii)', 7),
  ('3082e984-60b5-566e-94bc-9373327a205e', 'ea65b685-d0c0-5aa8-bb8d-d6bb01f68d36', 'Predicting match results', 'Calculations can be used to predict football match results. The probability of how many goals each team will score in the match is calculated using the Poisson distribution:

P(k; λ) = (λ^k · e^(−λ)) / k!  — that is, λ to the power k, multiplied by e to the power −λ, divided by k factorial.

Where:

- λ — the average expected number of goals (intensity).
- k — the number of goals.
- P(k; λ) — the probability that the team will score k goals.

The pseudocode for Poisson distribution is presented:

```pseudocode
VAR Ep REAL
VAR Poisson REAL
INPUT L
INPUT K
Lp = 1
FOR i from 1 to K DO
   Lp = Lp * L
ENDFOR
e = 2,71828
term = 1
FOR i from 1 to L DO
   term = term * e
ENDFOR
Ep = 1 / term
factorial = 1
FOR i from 1 to K DO
   factorial = factorial * i
ENDFOR
Poisson = (Lp * Ep) / factorial
OUTPUT K
```', 'structured', 7, 'exam', null, 'AI', 11, '90094a74-5e7b-589b-af06-e75a04fd67d7', 'c4201efe-ed79-5449-96aa-f264326baaf7', '{}'::jsonb, 'past_paper', 'NIS 2026 Paper 3 Q5', false, 'published', null, null, 0),
