- reason: share printers / files / Internet; central backup; log on anywhere; communication (1)', '[{"criterion":"Definition","marks":1},{"criterion":"Reason","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Two or more computers connected so they can communicate and share resources; the school can share one printer and Internet connection between all PCs.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('68b4c746-86bf-5b34-98a2-3f786d8cce47', 'e6436d06-a188-59fc-9a07-65b079633e52', 1, true, 'LAN; WAN; LAN; WAN; LAN (1 each)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 5","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('f03fc48f-fc42-52d1-a6a5-dbdea8b6572a', '30aad8ac-4577-55a8-9692-5fd9ab7fe7f0', 1, true, 'Any two comparative points mentioning both (1 each): area small vs large; owned by one organisation vs rented links; faster vs slower; fewer vs more errors; cheap vs expensive; cable / Wi-Fi vs fibre / satellite', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 A LAN covers a small area like a school, whereas a WAN covers a large area like a country. 2 A LAN is owned by one organisation, whereas a WAN uses links rented from telecom companies.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('0cf48d23-596b-5d35-95fd-7a80f960b843', '1bb6bb3b-4f47-5d6b-a62a-018274853165', 1, true, 'A', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"A"}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('8f96db35-b401-59d8-8633-4abe0adcf070', '3b435bfd-6712-547e-97c5-c288c36c8015', 1, true, '- A private network of one organisation (1)
- using Internet technologies (web pages, browsers, TCP/IP), accessible only to authorised users (1)', '[{"criterion":"Private, one organisation","marks":1},{"criterion":"Internet technology, authorised users","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A private network inside an organisation that uses web pages and Internet protocols but can only be used by its authorised members.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('14b315f9-d8de-552a-8505-4537c2d86dc7', '30fb314f-795f-571c-b534-e7d5e3402e19', 1, true, 'Internet; intranet; intranet; Internet (1 each)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('767f1158-f7c3-57f7-82ce-e082c57d5d23', '08214639-4203-593b-be4b-65e29bf566d6', 1, true, 'True.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":true}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('0e45af6d-dad5-542b-9b9b-d5cfe15cb2d1', '0e6e2487-6dd2-5b55-8d18-9515486aa76f', 1, true, 'CS; P2P; P2P; CS (1 each)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e35d0dc2-15ed-5d79-a727-c6579e84271c', '18064515-b29d-577a-8dd3-51f822215e2a', 1, true, 'Any three (1 each): central security — accounts / permissions / antivirus; central automatic backup; students can log on from any computer and see their files; easier to manage / install software for many PCs; performs better with many users', '[{"criterion":"Point 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Point 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Point 3","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The server controls user accounts and permissions, so security is managed centrally; all files are backed up automatically on the server; and students can log in from any of the 400 computers and reach their own files.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('1f8eac62-44c4-5ba9-a03d-6602f3954a2e', '36e6c066-4ff9-5768-b1b7-de012076075f', 1, true, 'Disadvantage (1) + explanation (1): no central backup — files on each PC can be lost; weak security — each user controls own PC; a switched-off peer cannot share files; slower with many users', '[{"criterion":"Disadvantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'There is no central backup, so if one computer fails, the files stored only on it are lost.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('8d34ccea-9d9b-56ee-a69f-cee600822955', 'df9a569b-3d05-5d84-9aba-092a8440913f', 1, true, 'L1–R1, L2–R2, L3–R3, L4–R4.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4"}}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('3aae8d73-a0ba-56b6-93d8-b73f9d8f3498', 'f6703438-bebd-5ab9-87a7-284adef47d17', 1, true, 'Advantages (1 each): mobility / customers can sit anywhere; phones and tablets can connect; no cables to install / cheaper / no trip hazard; easy to add many devices. Disadvantages (1 each): slower / speed varies; interference; signals can be intercepted — less secure; limited range', '[{"criterion":"Adv 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Adv 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Dis 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Dis 2","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Advantages: customers can connect from any seat; phones without network ports can connect. Disadvantages: the signals can be intercepted, so it is less secure; speed drops with many users and interference.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('b4dc06c9-4eb7-5a89-898c-97c5314ef741', '15b342b7-d65e-5d0f-a644-6fdf98c67836', 1, true, '- Copper twisted pair only works up to about 100 m; fibre carries signals over long distances (1)
- very high speed / no electrical interference / secure (1)', '[{"criterion":"Distance","marks":1},{"criterion":"Speed / interference","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Copper Ethernet only reaches about 100 m, but fibre carries light signals for kilometres at very high speed without electrical interference.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('48424cff-37ae-5a83-ad34-0206eba6d50e', '8cb34596-8e0f-5558-883c-a1220f775e8d', 1, true, 'Bus–R1, Ring–R2, Star–R3, Mesh–R4, Mixed–R5.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4","L5":"R5"}}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('608f13fa-42ad-56bb-b684-001f2e75e7f8', '5cb65a2f-84b6-5ddf-b814-a70d1e55a4ae', 1, true, 'Star; bus; mesh; ring; bus (1 each)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 5","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"","","✓",""],[null,"✓","","",""],[null,"","","","✓"],[null,"","✓","",""],[null,"✓","","",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('04f57e3a-fcbd-5404-abd3-0b9736a1c363', '0247fa3d-2e92-527e-9685-a815e7c69bfb', 1, true, 'Star adv: one cable failure affects only one device / easy to add devices / no collisions with switch / easy to find faults (1). Star dis: switch is a single point of failure / more cable / cost of switch (1). Bus adv: cheap / least cable / easy to add (1). Bus dis: backbone failure stops all / collisions / slow with many devices / hard to find faults (1)', '[{"criterion":"Star adv","marks":1},{"criterion":"Star dis","marks":1},{"criterion":"Bus adv","marks":1},{"criterion":"Bus dis","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Star: if one cable breaks, only that computer is affected; but if the switch fails, everything stops. Bus: cheap because it needs little cable; but a break in the backbone stops the whole network.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('f6a100e7-90dc-5b31-a2f9-9cbb091b4038', 'e4211d8e-5fbc-5012-9212-27cb066bd9ce', 1, true, '- Many routes between data centres / no single point of failure (1)
- if one link fails data is rerouted, so the bank''s services keep working / transactions are not lost (1)', '[{"criterion":"Many routes","marks":1},{"criterion":"Continues working","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'In a mesh there are many routes, so if one link fails, data is sent another way and the bank''s systems keep running without interruption.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('cc4534f9-d8fe-515a-be7f-b55ff934dfec', 'baaee198-4cb8-5a39-a82d-d9ee5dfd3ebd', 1, true, 'Mixed / hybrid (stars joined together; accept extended star / tree) (1)', '[{"criterion":"Mixed","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Mixed (hybrid) topology', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('8bbda493-d203-598b-bac6-58c20993f736', '33ed996a-4566-58a8-96c6-68d68056d6f2', 1, true, 'Advantage (1) + explanation (1): one broken cable affects only one PC, others keep working; easy to add PCs by plugging into the switch; switch sends data only to the destination → fast / secure', '[{"criterion":"Advantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Each PC has its own cable, so if one cable is damaged only that PC loses its connection and the rest of the room keeps working.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('b911577f-6bfa-5380-9249-8eb22e0d6b99', 'a1803420-c4f8-51fb-a086-347553eafb25', 1, true, 'PCs in each room still communicate with each other through their switch (1); but the two rooms / buildings cannot communicate, e.g. cannot reach a server in the other building (1)', '[{"criterion":"Rooms still work","marks":1},{"criterion":"No link between buildings","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Each room still works as its own star network, but the two buildings can no longer exchange data, so one building may lose access to the server or the Internet.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('b6a5a192-c538-5365-a502-ffddcc06ead7', '6fa4f93c-8a83-5880-b618-5d0e4c059a96', 1, true, 'Each comparison mentioning both (1 each): LAN small area / one building vs WAN large area / several cities; LAN owned by the company vs WAN uses links rented from telecom providers; LAN faster vs WAN slower / more latency; LAN cheap vs WAN expensive', '[{"criterion":"Area","marks":1},{"criterion":"Ownership","marks":1},{"criterion":"Speed","marks":1},{"criterion":"Cost","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Area: the LAN covers one office, whereas the WAN covers several cities. Ownership: the company owns the LAN, whereas the WAN uses lines rented from telecom companies. Speed: the LAN is faster than the WAN. Cost: the LAN is cheap, whereas the WAN is expensive to rent.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('f4a39cf1-4358-5544-b74c-f2176a52cb90', '7a735d98-dc9e-5cc5-b37f-19457a699c42', 1, true, 'Any three (1 each): private — only staff with logins can see; more secure / behind firewall; information controlled / reliable / up to date; internal information not visible to the public / competitors; faster access inside the network', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1},{"criterion":"3","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Only staff with a login can see the information, so it stays private; it is protected by the company firewall; and the company controls the content, so it is reliable and up to date.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('8c9fa772-7b79-58b1-a550-d7c3ce68a30d', '6fcb63e1-6d97-5902-9a60-1fc9bebbbad4', 1, true, 'Any three (1 each): central security / user accounts; central backup; files in one place / log on anywhere; easier management of 60 PCs / software updates; better performance for many users', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1},{"criterion":"3","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The server manages user accounts and permissions centrally, backs up all files automatically, and lets staff log in from any of the 60 computers to reach their files.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('ba311f14-28ed-56a3-b39e-a82b9b489e11', 'ac218bc3-fea0-5f42-8be0-b917e5c51ed9', 1, true, 'Wireless; wired; wireless; wired (1 each)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('04943f2a-4f19-5800-ad01-ab7ec39675f1', '396f172d-ddb8-52b5-bbca-359f6294d134', 1, true, 'Up to 4 (1 each): wired for server / desktops — fast, stable, secure for heavy data; desktops do not move so mobility not needed; Wi-Fi for laptops — mobility / meetings anywhere / no extra cables; drawback: Wi-Fi less secure → needs WPA2/WPA3 / strong password; drawback: Wi-Fi slower with many users; conclusion: sensible combination', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1},{"criterion":"3","marks":1},{"criterion":"4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Cabling the server and desktops is sensible: they don''t move and need fast, stable, secure connections. Wi-Fi suits laptops because staff move between rooms. However, Wi-Fi can be intercepted, so WPA3 encryption is needed, and it may slow down with many users. Overall it is a good balance.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('a515e94a-c35c-53b7-87b9-a0577c7464c0', 'c0237129-14b4-585d-91b7-0599097f9fda', 1, true, 'Bus: all on one backbone cable with terminators (1). Ring: each device connected to two others in a loop (1). Star: each device has its own link to a central switch / hub (1). Mesh: each device connected to several / all others (1)', '[{"criterion":"Bus","marks":1},{"criterion":"Ring","marks":1},{"criterion":"Star","marks":1},{"criterion":"Mesh","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Bus: every device joins one main cable. Ring: devices form a closed loop, each linked to two neighbours. Star: each device is cabled to a central switch. Mesh: devices are linked to many or all other devices.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('b16ee80e-e1ef-5cc1-ab59-df2004cc5b7d', 'e28f55b6-81be-5595-9d6d-f5e4c68c87b8', 1, true, 'Advantage: no collisions / equal access / good under heavy load (1). Disadvantage: one failed link or device stops the network / adding devices disrupts it / data passes through other devices (1)', '[{"criterion":"Advantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Disadvantage","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Advantage: no data collisions because only one device sends at a time. Disadvantage: if one link breaks, the whole ring stops.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('c3b5d80d-eb33-5865-991b-926ec67e916c', 'abd54cc9-4744-570a-a023-538504406b6e', 1, true, 'Recommend star (or justified alternative) (1); justification points (up to 3): one cable failure affects only one PC whereas bus backbone failure stops all; easy to add PCs; no collisions with switch / faster than bus with 60 PCs; cheaper and simpler than mesh; drawback acknowledged — switch single point of failure', '[{"criterion":"Recommendation","marks":1},{"criterion":"Justification 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Justification 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Comparison","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Star. Each PC has its own cable to a switch, so a broken cable affects only one PC, whereas in a bus a break in the backbone stops all 60 PCs. A switch sends data only to the destination, so there are no collisions, and new PCs are easy to add. It is also much cheaper than a mesh.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('4c283dad-0c62-598d-a096-8dec3c6cd678', '89a0f307-e466-5131-ab46-638efe041650', 1, true, 'Routers / networks are connected to many others (1); so there are many possible routes and data can be rerouted if a link fails (1)', '[{"criterion":"Many connections","marks":1},{"criterion":"Many routes","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Its routers are linked to many other routers, so there are many paths between any two points and data can go another way if one link fails.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null)
on conflict do nothing;

insert into public.mark_schemes (id, question_id, version, is_current, mark_scheme, marking_points, model_answer, accepted_answers, ai_grading_instructions, explanation) values
  ('d82f2777-032e-5daf-a791-ff03095366a5', '58144fec-c9ed-51e6-8d56-e3b01fd7dda6', 1, true, 'Questionnaire → written questions answered by many people; Interview → conversation with follow-up questions; Observation → watching users at work; Examining documents → studying forms, reports and records (1 each)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4"}}'::jsonb, null, 'These are the four fact-finding methods named in the specification.'),
  ('4fc154b9-9c5f-5f0e-ba59-c8d32f47bf84', '7b32fe74-b722-5680-bfbf-792c84253d7a', 1, true, 'C (1)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"C"}'::jsonb, null, 'A closed question has a fixed set of possible answers, so the answers can be counted (quantitative data).'),
  ('1e715cd6-6daa-5843-83d9-c8a2286bec3a', '7f3b2feb-4320-5d1d-9073-767e47607b7d', 1, true, 'False (1)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":false}'::jsonb, null, 'Closed questions have fixed answers that can be counted, so they produce quantitative data. Open questions produce qualitative data.'),
  ('80ee74d8-144e-53ff-b98d-5f11df26ddba', 'b3909c04-3408-5727-963f-eb4867516772', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): reaches many people; cheap; quick to collect; can be anonymous so answers may be more honest; closed answers are quick to analyse / easy to turn into statistics; people answer in their own time; online forms total the answers automatically', '[{"criterion":"First advantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different advantage","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 It can be given to many people at low cost. 2 It can be anonymous, so people may answer honestly.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('438b963f-f31e-5843-8e4b-a8ef9225d08b', 'd93b620b-3bff-5631-93a3-aaa9f6700e96', 1, true, 'Questionnaire (any two): low response rate; questions cannot be explained / may be misunderstood; limited depth / no follow-up questions; careless or untrue answers

Interview (any two): time-consuming; only a few people can be interviewed; expensive; not anonymous so answers may not be honest; depends on the interviewer''s skill; answers are harder to analyse', '[{"criterion":"Questionnaire disadvantage 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Questionnaire disadvantage 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Interview disadvantage 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Interview disadvantage 2","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Questionnaire: low response rate; questions cannot be explained. Interview: time-consuming so only a few people are interviewed; not anonymous so people may not be honest.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Each answer must apply to that method. Do not credit the same point twice in one method.', null),
  ('ae2f4bd0-7e62-5f60-a5eb-c7121d6c9ba0', 'd67dd193-05a5-5581-bc7d-60e4cf51884f', 1, true, 'Disadvantage (1) + explanation (1): people may behave differently when watched (1) so the analyst may not see how the system is normally used (1); time-consuming (1) because the analyst must watch for a long time / several days (1); rare events / problems may not be seen (1) so some problems are missed (1); does not show opinions (1) so reasons for problems are unknown (1)', '[{"criterion":"Disadvantage identified","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation of its effect","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Staff may work faster or more carefully when they know they are being watched, so the analyst does not see how the system is really used.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('61a877b2-6c47-5f71-a6b3-efcb523186e2', 'c289cc63-a99e-5afa-a0dd-e7d293fd39cd', 1, true, 'Any one (1): shows the exact data items / formats used; quick / cheap; does not disturb staff; shows the volume of data; gives facts for the data dictionary / screen design', '[{"criterion":"Valid advantage","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It shows exactly which data items are recorded on the current forms.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('5630eb6f-2f64-5408-a6a2-5425677bf16f', '9460439a-7f13-53f0-8b49-86693b451bf0', 1, true, 'Opinions of 500 students → questionnaire; director''s needs → interview; serving time → observation; data items on forms → examining documents (1 per row)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1 questionnaire","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2 interview","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3 observation","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4 documents","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓","","",""],[null,"","✓","",""],[null,"","","✓",""],[null,"","","","✓"]]}'::jsonb, null, 'Many people → questionnaire; one key person needing detail → interview; real times → observation; exact data items → documents.'),
  ('afb1ca2f-b79e-5ee8-9f67-fdc4fae05972', '2154b019-a3a4-5120-ad12-8639fbe55dab', 1, true, 'Structured → same questions in the same order; Semi-structured → prepared questions plus follow-ups; Unstructured → open conversation (1 each)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3"}}'::jsonb, null, 'Semi-structured interviews are the most common: they combine comparable answers with follow-up questions.'),
  ('c3e386b3-c557-595b-abe3-32d6db338576', 'b1a3e531-8e63-58b2-858f-32cd9a6af456', 1, true, 'B (1)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"B"}'::jsonb, null, 'A leading question pushes the person towards a particular answer, so the results are biased.'),
  ('c8daf254-7999-5f54-983b-4411967a7a90', '6a41c7b2-480d-51a5-be95-1fad82cd64c2', 1, true, 'Number of books → quantitative; opinions → qualitative; average time → quantitative; reasons → qualitative; ratings 1–5 → quantitative (1 each)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 5","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""]]}'::jsonb, null, 'Numbers, times, counts and ratings are quantitative; opinions and reasons in words are qualitative.'),
  ('ee57428e-796a-5b2e-b452-2dd083dd0b31', '79e47756-da57-5a59-a276-f43be30384f8', 1, true, '54 ÷ 120 × 100 (1) = 45% (1)', '[{"criterion":"Correct method 54/120 × 100","marks":1},{"criterion":"45%","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '54 ÷ 120 × 100 = 45%', '{"values":["45"],"numeric":true}'::jsonb, null, 'Percentage = part ÷ total × 100.'),
  ('d8f66d18-5d58-5883-bfcf-5ce149972d9d', '16de23e9-9445-5c19-9796-4ebc725bafc1', 1, true, 'Total 30 (1) ÷ 8 = 3.75 (1)', '[{"criterion":"Total of 30 / correct method","marks":1},{"criterion":"3.75","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '(4+5+3+4+2+4+5+3) ÷ 8 = 30 ÷ 8 = 3.75', '{"values":["3.75"],"numeric":true,"tolerance":0.005}'::jsonb, null, 'Mean = sum of all values ÷ number of values.'),
  ('476390d1-1292-5884-a4d4-4e8e74e6548a', '955134cc-0160-510f-acab-eff2005ee1b1', 1, true, '(1) themes (2) chart (3) triangulation', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"blanks":[["themes","theme","categories","groups"],["chart","graph","diagram"],["triangulation"]]}'::jsonb, null, 'Thematic analysis groups comments into themes; charts present numbers; triangulation compares results from different methods.'),
  ('991c2362-7628-53d4-936a-cf9047074097', 'e5b678af-3fcf-50ae-b700-6ced866b0f34', 1, true, 'Advantage (1): detailed / rich information; explains reasons and feelings; can reveal unexpected problems

Disadvantage (1): subjective / open to interpretation; slow / hard to analyse; usually a small sample; hard to compare or show in charts', '[{"criterion":"Valid advantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Valid disadvantage","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Advantage: it explains why users have problems. Disadvantage: it is slow to analyse and can be subjective.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('9003f655-4fa5-5c70-a1d8-895f4910977d', '7f0e5204-672d-5bee-9bb1-bd9023d7120b', 1, true, 'Up to 4 comparison points, each referring to both (1 each):
- quantitative uses numbers / qualitative uses words, opinions
- quantitative analysed with statistics, percentages, charts / qualitative by grouping into themes
- quantitative is objective and quick to analyse / qualitative is subjective and slow
- quantitative shows how many / how big a problem is / qualitative explains why
- quantitative works with large samples / qualitative usually small samples', '[{"criterion":"Comparison point 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Comparison point 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Comparison point 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Comparison point 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Quantitative analysis works with numbers such as counts and ratings, while qualitative analysis works with words such as opinions. Quantitative data is analysed with percentages and charts, qualitative data by grouping comments into themes. Quantitative analysis is quicker and more objective, but qualitative analysis gives more detail and explains why users have problems. Quantitative analysis can use large samples; qualitative analysis usually uses a few people.', '{}'::jsonb, 'A point only counts if it compares both methods (explicitly or with ''whereas''). Max 4.', null),
  ('4ada16a3-ea4a-5060-8ad8-1a766b98f50b', '27ff94f4-db54-506a-83cb-77ad54a02339', 1, true, '- A requirement about issuing books faster, e.g. using barcode scanning / automatic recording (1)
- that is specific / measurable, e.g. in under 10–30 seconds (1)', '[{"criterion":"Requirement that solves the slow issuing problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"Specific / measurable requirement","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The system must issue a book by scanning the book''s and the student''s barcodes in under 10 seconds.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('1b3a850a-9609-5c39-ab0c-0aa1d451d00a', 'a4b674fd-56dd-5123-aaa9-a8223aca0ff5', 1, true, '(1) methods (2) problems (3) solutions (4) requirements', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"blanks":[["methods","method","techniques"],["problems","problem","weaknesses"],["solutions","solution"],["requirements","requirement"]]}'::jsonb, null, 'Fact-finding → analysis of problems and needs → compare solutions → requirements specification.'),
  ('43bc7a59-a908-5b63-b551-1c9584a3a236', '3888fcb1-256a-58bd-b70b-62cb77a1cd25', 1, true, '4 × 3 = 12, 3 × 5 = 15, 5 × 2 = 10 (1 for at least two correct products) (1 for all three) → total 37 (1)', '[{"criterion":"At least two correct products","marks":1},{"criterion":"All three products correct","marks":1},{"criterion":"Total 37","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '4×3 + 3×5 + 5×2 = 12 + 15 + 10 = 37', '{"values":["37"],"numeric":true}'::jsonb, null, 'Multiply each score by the weight of its criterion and add the results.'),
  ('d74321d0-92aa-5168-a55c-46e87ce65441', '05452290-5541-5725-afff-65502c9e689a', 1, true, 'Any three (1 each): how well it meets the requirements; cost (purchase, development, training, running); time to introduce; hardware needed / compatibility; ease of use / training needed; support and updates; security; reliability; scalability / future growth; legal issues', '[{"criterion":"Criterion 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Criterion 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Criterion 3","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Cost. 2 How well it meets the requirements. 3 Time needed to introduce it.', '{}'::jsonb, 'The three criteria must be different.', null),
  ('31670e7a-4603-5d2c-a53a-af88b1c56b8f', '63129745-32a0-5ca3-82aa-7a6de8b2f6e3', 1, true, 'Comparison (max 3, each referring to both):
- off-the-shelf is cheaper / bespoke is expensive (1)
- off-the-shelf is available immediately / bespoke takes a long time to develop (1)
- bespoke matches the requirements exactly / off-the-shelf may lack features or include unneeded ones (1)
- off-the-shelf is widely tested with support / bespoke support only from the developer (1)

Recommendation (1): off-the-shelf, justified by the small budget, one-month deadline and common needs', '[{"criterion":"Comparison point 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Comparison point 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Comparison point 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Recommends off-the-shelf with a justification from the scenario","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Off-the-shelf booking software is cheaper and can be installed at once, whereas bespoke software is expensive and takes months to write. Bespoke software would match the clinic''s needs exactly, but the clinic''s needs are similar to other clinics, so off-the-shelf software will cover them. Off-the-shelf is recommended because of the small budget and the one-month deadline.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Comparison points must refer to both options. The recommendation mark needs a reason from the scenario.', null),
  ('264d9e12-1c38-5569-a146-ece6c0b47703', 'ea7e9608-7a36-5d7e-b639-752a9ad9fe94', 1, true, '- Binary search halves the number of records to check after each comparison (1)
- so at most about 13 comparisons are needed instead of up to 5000 with linear search / O(log n) vs O(n) (1)', '[{"criterion":"Binary search halves the search area each step","marks":1},{"criterion":"Comparison: about 13 vs up to 5000 comparisons / log n vs n","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Each comparison in a binary search discards half of the remaining records, so 5000 records need at most 13 comparisons, while a linear search may need to check all 5000.', '{}'::jsonb, null, '2¹³ = 8192 ≥ 5000, so the worst case is 13 comparisons.'),
  ('85bd8ce2-0990-566d-8196-26082eed3f92', '05e8299c-a587-5642-8bad-d70cdd4f7e55', 1, true, 'Add/delete records → functional; under 2 seconds → non-functional (performance); reminder emails → functional; password to edit → non-functional (security) (1 each)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"]]}'::jsonb, null, 'Functional requirements say what the system does; non-functional requirements say how well it must work (speed, security, usability).'),
  ('8c934c80-4051-5e98-9742-1df06ab6d4d5', 'd956bec2-b430-5881-a308-615b52bfee7a', 1, true, '- Rewritten with a measurable value, e.g. ''The timetable page must load in under 3 seconds'' (1)
