- objective and quick to analyse / subjective and slow
- shows how many or how big a problem is / explains why it happens
- large samples / small samples', '[{"criterion":"Comparison point 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Comparison point 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Comparison point 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Comparison point 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Quantitative analysis works with numbers such as counts and times, while qualitative analysis works with words such as opinions. Quantitative data is analysed with percentages and charts, qualitative data by grouping comments into themes. Quantitative analysis is quicker and more objective, but qualitative analysis explains why problems happen. Quantitative analysis suits large samples, qualitative analysis usually small ones.', '{}'::jsonb, 'A point counts only if it refers to both methods. Max 4.', null),
