  ('b929565f-3757-5656-af01-d5aadd8721d6', '2f18483f-e6ea-5e2c-9615-0567adc1c18a', 1, true, 'Up to 5 (1 each): user types URL / domain into browser; browser checks its cache / hosts file; request sent to DNS server / resolver which holds a list of domain names and IP addresses; if not found, request passed to other DNS servers (root → TLD → authoritative); IP address returned to the browser and cached; browser uses the IP address to contact the web server and request the page; error if name not found', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1},{"criterion":"3","marks":1},{"criterion":"4","marks":1},{"criterion":"5","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The user types the domain name in the browser, which first checks its cache. If the IP address is not there, it asks the DNS resolver, which looks it up and, if needed, asks a root server, then the .kz TLD server, then the domain''s authoritative server. The IP address is returned and cached, and the browser uses it to connect to the web server and request the page.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
