  ('f677fb44-502e-55f0-8e1b-b5fc0614c1e2', 'f3217f85-5293-5943-828e-5294183eccfb', 1, true, 'NIC connects the device to the network (1); MAC address uniquely identifies the device''s card so data can be delivered to it in the LAN (1)', '[{"criterion":"NIC","marks":1},{"criterion":"MAC","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The NIC lets the PC send and receive data on the network; its unique MAC address identifies the PC so the switch can deliver data to it.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('26a4c52f-f08a-55ef-b677-9c1352d02937', '3b24d6ed-1b2f-5db8-aa59-f943ffb4cc61', 1, true, 'Switch chosen (1); hub sends data to all devices (1); switch reads destination MAC and sends only to that device (1); benefit — less traffic / no collisions / faster / more secure (1)', '[{"criterion":"Switch","marks":1},{"criterion":"Hub behaviour","marks":1},{"criterion":"Switch behaviour","marks":1},{"criterion":"Benefit","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A switch. A hub sends every packet to all 31 devices, while a switch reads the MAC address and sends it only to the destination, so there is less traffic, no collisions and other students cannot see the data.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
