  ('5857ec4e-5eb4-5d24-aa21-a330133a84a3', '0792e887-d39e-50db-8090-008fd626e622', 1, true, 'Problems (max 2): patient / doctor details repeated — redundancy; update anomaly (phone / room change); insertion anomaly (new doctor with no visits); deletion anomaly
Normalisation (max 2): transitive dependencies — PatientPhone depends on patient, DoctorRoom on doctor; moved into separate tables
Final tables (max 2): Patients(PatientID, Name, Phone); Doctors(DoctorID, Name, Room); Visits(VisitID, VisitDate, PatientID*, DoctorID*, Diagnosis)', '[{"criterion":"Redundancy","marks":1},{"criterion":"Anomaly explained","marks":1},{"criterion":"Transitive dependency identified","marks":1},{"criterion":"How tables are split","marks":1},{"criterion":"Patients and Doctors tables","marks":1},{"criterion":"Visits with both FKs","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Each visit repeats the patient''s phone and the doctor''s room, which wastes space; if a doctor changes room, every visit row must be updated, and a new doctor cannot be stored until he has a visit. PatientPhone depends on the patient and DoctorRoom on the doctor, not on VisitID — transitive dependencies. Normalising to 3NF moves these into separate tables: Patients(PatientID, Name, Phone), Doctors(DoctorID, Name, Room) and Visits(VisitID, VisitDate, PatientID, DoctorID, Diagnosis), where PatientID and DoctorID are foreign keys.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
