  ('783e99e3-b0a0-5a41-84e6-70fd93d74b46', 'ef5d45f1-9fd0-549f-90b0-d7449f85ea91', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each):
- Allocates memory / RAM to programs and data when they are loaded
- Frees / deallocates memory when a program closes
- Protects memory so one program cannot access / overwrite another''s memory
- Uses virtual memory when RAM is full / moves pages between RAM and disk
- Keeps track of which parts of memory are in use', '[{"criterion":"First valid point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid point","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It allocates RAM to each program when it is loaded and frees it when the program closes, and it protects each program''s memory so that other programs cannot overwrite it.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
