  ('6f386b84-77cf-5cb9-b20c-e2d15b34c8c4', '2d570163-ac5c-5bfd-b366-064f09fda308', 1, true, 'Any three (1 each):
- The CPU can only execute one process at a time
- The scheduler gives each process a short time slice (e.g. round robin / by priority)
- When the time slice ends the OS saves the state of the process and loads the next one (context switch)
- Switching happens many times per second, so all programs appear to run simultaneously', '[{"criterion":"Only one process runs on the CPU at a time","marks":1},{"criterion":"Each process is given a time slice by the scheduler","marks":1},{"criterion":"Rapid switching / context switch makes them appear simultaneous","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The single CPU can only run one process at any moment. The scheduler gives each process a short time slice; when it ends, the OS saves that process''s state and switches to the next one. This switching happens so quickly, many times a second, that all the programs seem to run at the same time.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('00365211-48e7-5b69-9f08-cb460900438a', 'cf53bd8f-e7aa-531d-b37e-f51e39e102c1', 1, true, '- An OS that processes inputs / responds within a guaranteed / fixed (very short) time / deadline (1)
- so that it can control a physical process / system as it happens (1)', '[{"criterion":"Responds within a guaranteed time / deadline","marks":1},{"criterion":"To control a process / system immediately","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'An operating system that processes inputs and responds within a guaranteed, very short time, so that it can control a physical system as events happen.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('7191b3fe-0b22-5d67-a25f-290d36a3d2de', 'cbc3c658-19d0-5f32-a971-fa4879ac2321', 1, true, 'Airbag → Hard (1); Video streaming → Soft (1); Pacemaker → Hard (1); Online game → Soft (1)', '[{"criterion":"Airbag hard","marks":1},{"criterion":"Streaming soft","marks":1},{"criterion":"Pacemaker hard","marks":1},{"criterion":"Game soft","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"]]}'::jsonb, null, 'If a hard real-time deadline is missed the system fails and people may be hurt; a missed soft deadline only lowers quality.'),
  ('43781401-5b3a-58e1-b484-a5df215d707e', 'f3339db0-bb52-5690-a832-63e1845c618e', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): guaranteed response within a deadline; predictable / deterministic timing; priority-based pre-emptive scheduling — urgent tasks interrupt others; continuous monitoring of sensors with feedback; high reliability / fault tolerance / runs continuously; small and efficient / minimal user interface / embedded', '[{"criterion":"First valid feature","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid feature","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 It responds to inputs within a guaranteed deadline. 2 It uses priority scheduling, so the most urgent task can interrupt less important ones.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('b92d1521-86c4-512c-ad6d-5da0947af5a9', '3264e0c5-a3e7-5453-a635-f7fb64d9d810', 1, true, '- The airbag must inflate within a few milliseconds of the crash sensor detecting a collision / within a guaranteed time (1)
- otherwise it would inflate too late and the driver could be injured / it is safety-critical (1)', '[{"criterion":"Response within a guaranteed (very short) time is needed","marks":1},{"criterion":"Linked to safety: a late response could injure people","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The airbag must inflate within milliseconds of the sensor detecting a crash; if the response were late, the airbag would be useless and the driver could be injured.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('d5f15cdf-bf68-501a-9a23-bbd86c0b8f43', '43153588-1768-5580-8855-02b9f9361850', 1, true, 'A and C. One mark each; a mark is lost for each incorrect option selected.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":["A","C"]}'::jsonb, null, 'B is a feature of a real-time OS; D describes a single-tasking OS.'),
  ('bcc2a364-32b5-5932-b54c-a244d175f24a', '947d6231-bbed-5c1a-8f55-f4973265c8db', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each):
- NOS provides authentication and authorisation mechanisms…
- …ensuring that only authorised users can access network resources
- NOS verifies user identities (user name and password) when they log in…
- …to assign appropriate access rights (to a user or group)
[Max 2] 1 mark for mentioning authentication / authorisation', '[{"criterion":"Authenticates / verifies users at log-in","marks":1},{"criterion":"Assigns access rights / only authorised users access resources","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The NOS verifies each user''s identity with a user name and password when they log in, and then assigns access rights to that account, so only authorised users can reach each shared resource.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('35048e3d-414f-5173-be7c-c6174c52f440', 'd9c5d00a-babb-5060-8541-f64e69b0a446', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): jobs with similar requirements are batched together and run as a group; data is collected over a defined period of time and processed together; no user interaction while jobs run; data is sorted before processing; runs at off-peak times / scheduled automatically; suits large volumes of similar data', '[{"criterion":"First valid feature","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid feature","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Jobs with similar requirements are grouped into a batch and run together. 2 The batch runs without any user interaction, often at night.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('3c72d252-824d-5266-bde9-b5c6a35f0838', '89eff04b-a1db-5734-88af-bc5cb807c179', 1, true, 'False.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":false}'::jsonb, null, 'Batch jobs run without user interaction; the instructions and data are prepared in advance.'),
  ('ca9cc59f-3f4c-57cd-ab33-9aa9b445fe5c', '18bf426e-2e0a-5dd2-b0d7-91202dc77fef', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each):
