  ('f3fe7123-4b73-5043-badd-0d9e4e4c4837', '2f91420f-5fc2-5412-9673-923ca3d31557', 1, true, 'ABS → Real-time (1); School server → Network (1); Payslips → Batch (1); Robot → Real-time (1)', '[{"criterion":"ABS real-time","marks":1},{"criterion":"School server network","marks":1},{"criterion":"Payslips batch","marks":1},{"criterion":"Robot real-time","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓","",""],[null,"","✓",""],[null,"","","✓"],[null,"✓","",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('4374437f-6ff0-5f1d-a0a8-2d006160d8fa', '6d642ae0-c1c1-53ce-a3ec-6ab83177da1e', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each), both sides needed:
- Batch processes data later in groups, whereas real-time processes data immediately as it arrives
- Batch has no user interaction during processing, whereas real-time responds to inputs continuously
- Batch suits large volumes where results are not urgent (bills), whereas real-time suits control / urgent systems (airbag, booking)', '[{"criterion":"First valid comparison","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second valid comparison","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Batch processing collects data and processes it later as a group without user interaction, whereas real-time processing handles each input immediately. Batch suits large non-urgent jobs such as monthly bills, while real-time suits control systems such as an airbag.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('d831d48f-4d35-5d0e-9bd1-656bdfa59e59', 'a1ba60f5-c33f-543f-9c77-11a47ac6bfa3', 1, true, 'For each of two jobs: type (1) + justification (1).
- Job 1: real-time (1) — must respond within a guaranteed time / safety-critical, a delayed alarm could cost a life (1)
- Job 2: network OS (1) — central user accounts / authentication / access rights to shared records for many users (1)
- Job 3: batch (1) — large volume of similar records, not urgent, run overnight without interaction (1)
[Max 4]', '[{"criterion":"Correct type for the first job","marks":1},{"criterion":"Justification for the first job","marks":1},{"criterion":"Correct type for the second job","marks":1},{"criterion":"Justification for the second job","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Job 1 needs a real-time OS, because the alarm must sound within a guaranteed time and a delay could endanger the patient. Job 2 needs a network OS, because it manages the 600 user accounts centrally and gives each member of staff access rights to the shared records.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Mark the best two jobs. A justification only scores if it matches the chosen type.', null),
  ('f6668929-98cf-5b4f-81d4-7a3e6b7971e2', '0f0efca8-23d1-55f4-9830-13a04ff066ef', 1, true, '- The positions of aircraft change continuously and must be processed within a guaranteed time / immediately (1)
- so controllers see up-to-date positions and collisions are avoided / safety-critical (1)', '[{"criterion":"Data processed within a guaranteed time","marks":1},{"criterion":"Linked to safety / up-to-date positions","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Aircraft positions change every second and must be processed immediately, so that controllers always see the current positions and can prevent collisions.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('669371ba-9444-5bbe-bed2-33b00b3e1cba', '1235dd39-2bf7-5ffe-bdee-80b5fe50c97d', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): user account management / authentication; access rights / authorisation; file sharing; printer sharing; centralised backup; security / firewall / logging; remote administration; supports many users at once', '[{"criterion":"First valid feature","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid feature","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 It authenticates staff when they log in to their accounts. 2 It lets staff share files and printers on the network.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('efb6fc5a-c570-5d1c-a93e-7daa51f0c572', '73b9b2e2-546f-5f4f-bd23-09a36152a117', 1, true, '- Salaries of all staff are similar jobs that are calculated together once a month (1)
- results are not needed immediately, so the batch can run automatically without interaction / overnight (1)', '[{"criterion":"Many similar jobs processed together","marks":1},{"criterion":"Not urgent / runs without interaction","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'All the salaries are similar calculations that are only needed once a month, so they can be grouped and processed together automatically overnight.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('a015b490-043e-58b9-9650-7e6a4a9c0814', 'caff5b14-068f-5156-98a7-7e7e24d70bdb', 1, true, 'Comparison points (max 4):
- single-user: one user at a time; multi-user: many users share resources at once (1)
- multitasking: several programs share the CPU using time slices (1)
- real-time: guaranteed response within a deadline; priority scheduling (1)
- multi-user needs strong security / resource sharing; real-time minimal UI / high reliability (1)

Recommendations (max 2, need all three for 2, two for 1):
- laptops: single-user multitasking
- server: multi-user (network) OS
- machine controller: real-time', '[{"criterion":"Valid comparison of single-user and multi-user","marks":1},{"criterion":"Valid description of multitasking","marks":1},{"criterion":"Valid description of real-time","marks":1},{"criterion":"Further valid comparison point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Two correct recommendations","marks":1},{"criterion":"All three recommendations correct and justified","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A single-user OS allows one person to use the computer at a time, while a multi-user OS lets many people share one computer''s processor, memory and storage at once, so it needs stronger security to keep their data apart. A multitasking OS runs several programs at once by giving each a time slice of the CPU. A real-time OS responds to inputs within a guaranteed deadline using priority scheduling, and usually has little user interface. The laptops should use a single-user multitasking OS so employees can run several programs; the server should use a multi-user network OS so 200 staff can log in and share resources; the machine controller needs a real-time OS because it must react to sensors immediately.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('7275de32-f5f8-5311-b295-f73a507f48ed', '39feebaa-71b9-552e-af6f-72a9780683de', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): allocates RAM to each program; protects each program''s memory from the others; frees memory when a program closes; uses virtual memory if RAM is full; keeps track of used and free memory', '[{"criterion":"First valid point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid point","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It gives each of the three programs its own part of RAM and stops them from overwriting each other''s memory; if RAM becomes full it uses virtual memory on the disk.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('2bb26d3c-31b3-5500-8ec6-27405b4832dd', 'cf03f78e-1d2f-5e2c-b4c7-ea03d62f8a6c', 1, true, 'Any three (1 each):
- It is a multitasking OS
- The CPU runs only one process at a time
- The scheduler gives each program a time slice
- The OS saves the state of one process and loads the next (context switch)
- Switching is so fast that the programs appear to run simultaneously', '[{"criterion":"First valid point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second valid point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third valid point","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The multitasking OS gives each program a short time slice of the CPU in turn. When a slice ends it saves that program''s state and switches to the next one, and it does this so quickly that the essay, the music and the download all appear to run at the same time.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('469f9755-27e6-5f0b-bf06-d3616fb474e2', '466ca331-b207-5863-a1c4-d18cab8a3282', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each), described: file management; input/output / peripheral management through drivers; security / user accounts / access rights; providing a user interface; error handling; loading and running applications; handling interrupts', '[{"criterion":"First valid function described","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid function described","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 File management — it saves Madina''s essay in a folder and records where it is stored on the disk. 2 It provides a graphical user interface so she can open programs with the mouse.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Do not credit memory management or processor scheduling. A function name alone with no description is not enough.', null),
  ('092160b7-a001-5704-ab58-037bff0dd301', 'c364eca6-1aed-59b6-b29d-88c733050b02', 1, true, 'Water bills → Batch (1); Aircraft engine → Real-time (1); Office folders and printers → Network (1)', '[{"criterion":"Bills batch","marks":1},{"criterion":"Engine real-time","marks":1},{"criterion":"Office network","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"","","✓"],[null,"✓","",""],[null,"","✓",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('70102466-269c-52ec-8dd0-9f89932ab374', '12ad7533-caeb-5f78-a7b1-6ca9fee0c2b0', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each), both sides needed: one user at a time vs many users simultaneously; all resources for one user vs resources shared between users (time-sharing); simpler security vs strong security to separate users'' data; PC / laptop vs mainframe / server', '[{"criterion":"First valid comparison","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second valid comparison","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A single-user OS lets only one person use the computer at a time, whereas a multi-user OS lets many people use it at once. The multi-user OS must share CPU time and memory between the users and keep each user''s data secure.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('c505214b-8723-5702-82c8-00f8ad7f479e', 'aa3eb829-474d-526b-a008-24516e72813b', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): jobs with similar requirements are batched together and run as a group; data collected for a defined period and processed as a pack; sorting is performed before processing; no user interaction; runs at off-peak / scheduled times', '[{"criterion":"First valid feature","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid feature","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Jobs with similar requirements are grouped together and run as one batch. 2 The jobs run without any interaction with the user.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('307ca198-4ba7-5178-83d0-07a177e15a67', 'b71cc2b3-4d21-5380-94fc-0b87ead043d3', 1, true, '- Processes inputs / responds within a guaranteed time / deadline (1)
- to control a system as events happen (1)', '[{"criterion":"Guaranteed response time","marks":1},{"criterion":"Controls a system as events happen","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'An OS that processes inputs and responds within a guaranteed time so that it can control a system as events happen.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('beb4d327-badb-5aa7-a8ee-3e54cfea554a', '98068965-7007-5258-b688-af58de521c59', 1, true, '- Every deadline must be met / response must always be within the time limit (1)
- missing a deadline means system failure / could injure the passengers (1)', '[{"criterion":"Deadlines must always be met","marks":1},{"criterion":"Missing one is a failure / dangerous","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The airbag must always respond within its deadline; if it ever responds late, the system has failed and the passengers could be injured.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('aff6926f-1f88-5d92-9481-dcbe082c3ec5', '1d9b2355-272d-52d7-8cc6-79bdb01ac356', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): priority-based pre-emptive scheduling; deterministic / predictable; continuous monitoring of sensors with feedback; high reliability / fail-safe / runs continuously; small / efficient / embedded in ROM; minimal user interface', '[{"criterion":"First valid feature","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid feature","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 It uses priority scheduling, so the most urgent task interrupts others. 2 It is highly reliable and runs continuously without failing.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Do not credit ''responds quickly / within a deadline'' — it is excluded by the question.', null),
  ('d14b50fc-3c68-5308-af6a-38ea60bea104', '256f225b-444e-5363-b1a6-c44f818f4c9c', 1, true, '- In a soft real-time system a missed deadline only reduces quality / is not dangerous, e.g. the music or map updates late (1)
- In a hard real-time system a missed deadline is a failure / dangerous, e.g. the airbag / ABS (1)', '[{"criterion":"Soft: missed deadline reduces quality, with car example","marks":1},{"criterion":"Hard: missed deadline is failure / dangerous, with car example","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'If the navigation screen misses a deadline, the map just updates a little late, which is annoying but not dangerous. If the airbag or ABS misses a deadline, the system fails and people could be hurt.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('fb64540e-6ea3-594d-bbcd-5abfd639ff5e', '19839f27-a319-56eb-940d-1518c2b2384b', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): provides authentication and authorisation mechanisms; ensures that only authorised users can access network resources; verifies user identities (user name / password) at log-in; assigns appropriate access rights to users / groups
[Max 2]', '[{"criterion":"Authenticates users","marks":1},{"criterion":"Assigns access rights / authorisation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The NOS checks each pupil''s user name and password when they log in and then gives their account the access rights for their group, so only authorised users can open each shared resource.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('2225678d-6554-5de3-8513-121df8307b78', '630544f4-a567-5e4e-8361-1be60a2e33d3', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): file sharing; printer sharing / print queues; centralised backup; security / firewall / activity logs; remote administration / software updates for clients; network services (DHCP, DNS, e-mail)', '[{"criterion":"First valid feature","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid feature","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 It lets pupils share files stored on the server. 2 It backs up all the users'' work centrally.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Do not credit user accounts / authentication again.', null),
  ('01b9fb62-96fa-55e1-95d3-0924dffb4531', '98201297-3ad2-5003-b7c0-e95041a94789', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): large number of similar jobs; transactions collected during the month and processed together; statements not needed immediately; can run automatically at night / off-peak without interaction', '[{"criterion":"First valid reason","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second valid reason","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Every customer''s statement is a similar job, and the transactions collected during the month are only needed once a month, so they can be processed together automatically overnight.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e9aafc73-f7fb-538d-80ab-8e43449cadf6', 'fb7a61a2-a415-56d4-bc21-0b93f5e8dd26', 1, true, 'Disadvantage (1) + explanation (1), e.g.
- Results are not immediate (1) so balances / statements are out of date until the batch runs (1)
- An error may only be found after the whole batch has been processed (1) so all statements may have to be produced again (1)
- No interaction during processing (1) so a job cannot be corrected while running (1)', '[{"criterion":"Valid disadvantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation linked to the bank","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The results are not immediate, so a customer''s statement does not show transactions until the batch has been run at the end of the month.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('3f476442-7f77-5e6b-a230-c9e12f20b8f8', '6de2905a-558b-55ba-86db-ae39812ae850', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): unique address of a device on the network; used to send and receive data / route packets to the device; identifies and locates the device', '[{"criterion":"Unique address","marks":1},{"criterion":"Send / receive / locate","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It is a unique address for a device on a network, used so that data packets can be delivered to and from that device.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
