  ('ab247ca3-865b-5613-aaa3-4e12db125420', 'f3b677a5-3ab7-5e33-b355-1b9f38f6e043', 1, true, 'Up to 5 (1 each): photo split into packets with headers; routers read destination IP; forward along best available route using routing tables / hops; packets may take different routes / arrive out of order; at the destination network MAC address used to deliver to the server; errors checked / missing packets requested again; packets reassembled in order using sequence numbers', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1},{"criterion":"3","marks":1},{"criterion":"4","marks":1},{"criterion":"5","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The photo is split into packets, each with the server''s IP address and a sequence number. Each router reads the destination IP and sends the packet to the next router on the best route, so packets may travel different ways and arrive out of order. In Almaty the last router delivers the frames to the server''s MAC address. The server checks for errors, asks for missing packets again and puts them back in order using the sequence numbers.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('ae587f05-e666-5198-9ac9-d49ab9d9fcc7', '9a2d3b12-ab9d-5365-8e2f-7e08c5e0cf6a', 1, true, 'SMTP — sending e-mail (1). HTTP — transferring web pages over the Internet (1)', '[{"criterion":"SMTP","marks":1},{"criterion":"HTTP","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'SMTP: sending e-mail.
HTTP: transferring web pages from a server to a browser.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('f3844c60-7dbc-526d-9bad-b4df8ea1b7e5', '22501db9-1cdc-5439-82ee-c344c729a93e', 1, true, 'FTPS (accept SFTP) (1); transfers files between client and server with encryption so the login and files cannot be intercepted (1)', '[{"criterion":"FTPS","marks":1},{"criterion":"Reason","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'FTPS — it transfers files to the server like FTP but encrypts the password and data.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('939ef943-56db-5453-841a-19a387d4ca89', 'c660c422-cdbf-583b-832e-67028b732639', 1, true, 'IMAP (1); messages stay on the server and are synchronised (1); POP3 downloads to one device and usually deletes from the server, so the other device would not see them (1)', '[{"criterion":"IMAP","marks":1},{"criterion":"Stays on server","marks":1},{"criterion":"POP3 problem","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'IMAP, because messages stay on the server and both devices show the same folders; with POP3 the messages would be downloaded to one device and removed from the server.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('2eec0aad-ee13-583c-bff5-786bb50e5b8f', '41ba771b-5d84-5caf-a0af-d5fc43849df8', 1, true, 'TCP/IP–R1, FTP–R2, POP3–R3.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3"}}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('51295b47-ed01-5dfe-a9dc-1b2e371437c1', '17ee3a78-1fa3-5878-8c84-4f5d8fab4300', 1, true, 'FTP resends lost / damaged packets and reassembles them so files arrive complete (1); this causes delays, unsuitable for live streaming (1)', '[{"criterion":"Reliable","marks":1},{"criterion":"Delay","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'FTP makes sure every packet arrives and is reassembled correctly, which is right for files, but resending and reordering cause delays that interrupt a live video.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
