  ('7a13b94c-d1e5-5596-88a8-85a030763ae1', '072a0dab-2207-5c4f-b071-b74ddf2accbc', 1, true, 'Client code is visible to users (1); database username / password would be exposed, server keeps them secret / database is on the server (1)', '[{"criterion":"Client code visible","marks":1},{"criterion":"Credentials secure","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'JavaScript code can be seen by anyone, so the database password would be revealed; PHP runs on the server, so the password and the database stay hidden.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('ae279114-4c07-510e-9ff4-eecfea8e4fe9', 'f9dcfd69-c563-56b6-a456-c407d7860a10', 1, true, 'B', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"B"}'::jsonb, null, 'The problem is investigated (analysis) before the solution is planned (design), built (development), checked (testing) and installed (implementation).'),
  ('3b5da108-70e0-5bf7-8e8d-5831a04d01ad', 'af14295c-89f0-556a-beb2-19634b517e16', 1, true, 'Requirements specification (accept: system requirements / requirements document / user requirements).', '[{"criterion":"Requirements specification or equivalent","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A requirements specification.', '{"values":["requirements specification","requirement specification","requirements document","system requirements","requirements specification document","system requirements specification","user requirements"]}'::jsonb, null, 'Analysis investigates the problem and records what the new system must do in a requirements specification, which is the input to the design stage.'),
  ('8bfc29a4-1b4d-5df7-974f-b92631f108c8', '71900ed2-7e25-5821-9e4d-d35c7a308611', 1, true, 'Analysis–R1, Design–R2, Testing–R3, Maintenance–R4. One mark per correct match.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4"}}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('fb53adf1-a4ff-5ab7-89a3-978b6912d0ef', '919c5436-df7d-519f-8bb5-2d17868918fe', 1, true, 'False.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":false}'::jsonb, null, 'Fixed, signed-off requirements are a feature of the waterfall model. Agile expects requirements to change and adapts the plan after each iteration.'),
  ('1f6f9adf-e3fa-5c5d-baad-160dcb5c0cb6', 'd980a246-8009-560a-84c4-873730d0ba40', 1, true, 'C', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"C"}'::jsonb, null, 'Risk analysis in each loop is the defining characteristic of the spiral model.'),
  ('f30ede34-e123-5b2f-8339-730115c76112', '7ba635b7-bbe6-5aba-a14d-4b06c532ac6b', 1, true, 'A and C. One mark each; a mark is lost for each incorrect option selected.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":["A","C"]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('c0682508-9cea-537b-8763-76e916fa32f3', 'a6f96827-925a-5b58-a4ef-4b0066ca5a3e', 1, true, '1 mark for identifying an advantage; 1 mark for explaining why it is an advantage / how it arises.

Examples:
- Can respond to changing requirements (1) because the plan is reviewed after each short iteration (1).
- Client sees working parts early (1) so misunderstandings are found and corrected before much time/money is wasted (1).
- Working parts can be used before the project ends (1) because each iteration delivers a usable increment (1).', '[{"criterion":"Identifies a valid advantage of agile over waterfall","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explains why/how this advantage arises (expansion linked to iterations or client feedback)","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Agile can cope with changing requirements, because the system is built in short iterations and the client reviews each one, so new or changed requirements can be included in the next iteration instead of having to restart the project.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Award the second mark only if the expansion explains the mechanism (short iterations, regular client feedback, incremental delivery). A second advantage without expansion does not earn the second mark.', null),
  ('a875d776-2582-559a-b07e-16296e5222c6', 'da3e7b10-f30e-5441-ae09-d372c82124eb', 1, true, 'Up to 4 marks. Expected choice: **spiral** (accept a well-justified alternative, maximum 3 marks).

- Identifies spiral as most suitable (1)
- Justification linked to risk: risk analysis in every loop reduces the danger of errors in a safety-critical system (1)
- Justification linked to size/cost: suitable for large, expensive projects (1)
- Justification linked to unclear requirements: prototypes/iterations allow requirements to be refined (1)
- Comparison point: why waterfall (fixed requirements) or agile (less up-front risk analysis/documentation) is less suitable (1)', '[{"criterion":"Chooses the spiral model (or a justified alternative)","marks":1},{"criterion":"Links risk analysis to the safety-critical nature of the system","marks":1},{"criterion":"Links model to the large/expensive scale of the project","marks":1},{"criterion":"Links iterations/prototypes to the requirements that are not fully understood","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explains why another model is less suitable","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The spiral model is most suitable. Because errors could endanger patients, the risk-analysis phase in every loop means hazards are identified and reduced before each new part is built. The project is large and expensive, which is the kind of project spiral is designed for. As some requirements are unclear, each loop can produce a prototype that doctors evaluate, refining the requirements. Waterfall would be unsuitable because it needs all requirements fixed at the start, and agile performs less formal risk analysis and documentation, which a safety-critical system needs.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Maximum 4 marks. Points must be applied to the hospital scenario; generic statements about a model that are not linked to the scenario earn at most 1 mark in total. If the student chooses agile or waterfall, award a maximum of 3 marks for justification that is accurate and linked to the scenario.', 'A ''discuss'' question needs a decision and justification applied to the context, ideally with a counter-point about the alternatives.'),
  ('f74180d8-59eb-58ef-8b03-ae3ad7292504', 'f70042e5-d3d9-58b6-a2b7-1cdd71a183bb', 1, true, '- A structured sequence of stages / steps (1)
- followed to plan, develop, implement and maintain a (new) information system (1)', '[{"criterion":"A structured sequence of stages","marks":1},{"criterion":"Used to plan, build, introduce and maintain a system","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A structured sequence of stages that is followed to plan, build, introduce and maintain a new information system.', '{}'::jsonb, null, 'The SDLC breaks a project into stages — analysis, design, development and testing, implementation, documentation, evaluation and maintenance.'),
  ('4b5cb41b-018c-5c74-8e56-d84d4349f4a9', 'fe20a9fb-8dc5-50c2-be2f-954266556eac', 1, true, 'B — Analysis (1)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"B"}'::jsonb, null, 'The feasibility study is part of analysis: before designing anything, the team checks that the project is technically, economically, legally, operationally and schedule-wise possible.'),
  ('124b8581-1f26-56e2-ac6a-583f0d9b1525', '573e3c35-51e4-5550-9977-8a51224a3378', 1, true, 'Technical → hardware/software/skills exist; Economic → benefits outweigh costs; Legal → follows the law; Operational → users able and willing to use it; Schedule → finished by the deadline (1 each)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4","L5":"R5"}}'::jsonb, null, 'TELOS = Technical, Economic, Legal, Operational, Schedule.'),
  ('b6aacc63-5d16-5876-a880-afe72f8f5d09', '42a0709a-741f-5867-b3c9-91566a4bd24a', 1, true, 'A, B, D (1 each)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":["A","B","D"]}'::jsonb, null, 'ERDs, the data dictionary and the test plan are design documents. The feasibility report belongs to analysis, the user guide to documentation, and the evaluation report to evaluation.'),
  ('fe395469-3cca-5a5b-ac8d-3cab05468fd7', '2c2aa61b-a39d-53a2-85f2-3eb61a837811', 1, true, '(1) analysis (2) design (3) implementation', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"blanks":[["analysis","analysis stage"],["design","design stage"],["implementation","implementation stage"]]}'::jsonb, null, 'Analysis investigates the current system; design produces the plans (ERD, data dictionary, layouts); implementation installs the system, transfers data and trains users.'),
  ('f21274ef-85c5-515f-a1e1-e0155b7be109', 'ef911853-bccc-590c-929f-b0428abd03ec', 1, true, 'Alpha → developers'' own team in-house; Beta → limited group of real users before full release; Acceptance → the client confirms requirements are met (1 each)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3"}}'::jsonb, null, 'Alpha testing is in-house, beta testing uses real users before release, acceptance testing is done by the client to accept the system.'),
  ('05863e4c-cfec-55fc-befc-18fae97adcd8', 'aff64f4d-db36-5171-8e2f-246741e04cba', 1, true, '1 Corrective (1)
2 Adaptive (1)
3 Perfective (1)', '[{"criterion":"Bug fix → corrective","marks":1},{"criterion":"Change of tax law → adaptive","marks":1},{"criterion":"New feature requested by users → perfective","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"corrective||corrective maintenance"],[null,"adaptive||adaptive maintenance"],[null,"perfective||perfective maintenance"]]}'::jsonb, null, 'Corrective fixes errors; adaptive changes the system for a new environment (law, OS, hardware); perfective improves or adds features.'),
  ('eb84bc71-e7fc-549e-96e7-f75e879240bb', 'd9c5743d-13e6-5d10-823a-90b7142d1675', 1, true, 'Technical (1): program code / comments, algorithms or flowcharts, data dictionary, ERD/DFD, hardware and software requirements, test results

User (1): how to install / log in, how to carry out tasks, screenshots, error messages and what to do, FAQ / troubleshooting, backup procedures', '[{"criterion":"Valid technical documentation item","marks":1},{"criterion":"Valid user documentation item","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Technical: the data dictionary. User: step-by-step instructions on how to log in.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Each box is marked separately; the item must belong to that type of documentation.', null),
  ('b27105a5-1190-56d3-8c20-97a982cacae3', 'beb84bc1-1c7a-5bb4-bb4f-ae1a14f26d49', 1, true, '- The finished system is compared against the requirements (1)
- to decide whether it does everything it should / whether the project succeeded / to identify improvements (1)', '[{"criterion":"The system is compared with the requirements","marks":1},{"criterion":"To check whether all requirements are met / project succeeded / find improvements","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The new system is compared with each requirement in the specification to decide whether it meets the client''s needs and what still needs to be improved.', '{}'::jsonb, null, 'Specific, testable requirements make evaluation objective.'),
  ('b80a29dd-96f1-596d-ab74-a7103416b9cf', '1d805e20-2810-5a5b-9dc1-188b6c5a258b', 1, true, 'True (1)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":true}'::jsonb, null, 'Waterfall is sequential: implementation (coding) is completed before the testing stage starts, so errors are often found late.'),
  ('3126daa1-0e5a-5145-b2e4-986b80febc38', 'aecba9b2-9b9d-5147-bb4f-77c59e767151', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): clear / simple structure; each stage is completed before the next starts; easy to manage with clear milestones; cost and time easy to estimate; thorough documentation at each stage; suitable when requirements are clear and fixed', '[{"criterion":"First valid benefit","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid benefit","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Clear structure — each stage is completed before the next begins. 2 Cost and time are easier to estimate.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Do not credit the same benefit twice.', null),
  ('5c8545aa-ded9-5ef1-80fb-f9cba30b7fa1', '09c04686-69ba-56a0-bae3-9e7044165ca8', 1, true, 'Product owner → decides priorities for the client; Scrum master → removes obstacles; Sprint → 1–4 week cycle producing working software; Daily stand-up → short daily meeting (1 each)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4"}}'::jsonb, null, 'Scrum is an agile method: work is done in sprints; the product owner prioritises the backlog; the scrum master keeps the process running; the team meets briefly every day.'),
  ('cad39bb0-b8a8-579e-ab26-8724c66fcf00', 'aa6fbb0e-2614-5c84-93fe-5667dc313937', 1, true, 'C (1)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"C"}'::jsonb, null, 'Each sprint delivers a working increment that the client reviews; the final system is built up over many sprints.'),
  ('3c95de2b-bd2a-598d-94c9-81d97759d6c5', '628bc6f0-84b7-54a7-b1d1-8adb2683eff8', 1, true, 'Any one explained point (2): the client must attend reviews regularly (1) which takes a lot of their time (1); requirements keep changing (1) so the final cost / deadline is hard to predict (1); less documentation (1) so later maintenance may be harder / more expensive (1)', '[{"criterion":"Identifies a disadvantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explains its consequence for the client","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The client has to take part in a review at the end of every sprint, which takes up a lot of their time over the whole project.', '{}'::jsonb, 'The second mark needs a consequence linked to the client.', null),
  ('03ac7104-9398-563c-8b10-3e44987fbea7', 'bd43b43f-8c61-5cd1-bde8-fc1c717c3fe3', 1, true, '(1) objectives (2) risks (3) test (4) plan', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"blanks":[["objectives","objective","requirements"],["risks","risk"],["test","testing"],["plan","planning"]]}'::jsonb, null, 'Objectives → risk analysis (often with a prototype) → develop and test → evaluate and plan the next loop.'),
  ('b166176f-d174-5b71-9860-aff3d6fb4695', 'cddbc411-cd17-5735-a1d8-19ab2d820906', 1, true, '- Risk analysis in every loop is expensive / needs specialists (1)
- which is not worth the cost when the project is small / risks are low (1)
- the process is complex to manage / many loops for a simple system (1)

Max 2', '[{"criterion":"Risk analysis / loops are expensive or complex","marks":1},{"criterion":"Not justified for a small, low-risk project","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Each loop needs a risk analysis carried out by specialists, which is expensive and complex; for a small, low-risk project that cost is not justified, so a simpler model such as waterfall is better.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('3287afc6-328b-5e62-9ab5-cbed20ffe4d1', 'c49ac5cf-e0c3-5535-9e61-43dbf09e7809', 1, true, 'Risk analysis in every loop → Spiral; Requirements fixed at the start → Waterfall; Working software every 1–4 weeks → Agile; Each stage signed off before the next → Waterfall (1 per row)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1: spiral","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2: waterfall","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3: agile","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4: waterfall","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"","","✓"],[null,"✓","",""],[null,"","✓",""],[null,"✓","",""]]}'::jsonb, null, 'Spiral is risk-driven, agile delivers in sprints, waterfall fixes requirements and completes stages in order.'),
  ('e6f57060-777b-55bd-8bd8-95fe1ff36f7b', '536bf5b4-69ed-553a-8da2-da0ada988a1b', 1, true, 'B — Agile (1)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"B"}'::jsonb, null, 'Agile handles changing requirements through short sprints with regular feedback from users.'),
  ('087cd7ae-b1c1-5f66-917b-0322f7f4570c', 'd81aff5c-3e60-5460-bf46-ee852f457200', 1, true, 'Waterfall points (max 2): simple to manage, clear milestones, good documentation (1); but requirements must be fixed at the start / changes are hard (1); teachers would only see the system at the end (1)

Agile points (max 2): requirements can change between sprints (1); teachers see and test working versions early and give feedback (1); final cost and time less predictable / needs teachers'' time (1)

Recommendation (max 2): agile (1) because requirements are incomplete and teachers want to try versions and suggest changes (1)', '[{"criterion":"Valid point about waterfall","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second valid point about waterfall (advantage or disadvantage)","marks":1},{"criterion":"Valid point about agile","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second valid point about agile","marks":1},{"criterion":"Recommends agile","marks":1},{"criterion":"Justification linked to the scenario","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Waterfall is easy to manage and well documented, but it needs all requirements fixed at the start and teachers would only see the system at the end. Agile lets requirements change between sprints and gives teachers working versions to test early, although its final cost and deadline are harder to predict. Agile is recommended, because the deputy head cannot describe all the requirements yet and teachers want to try early versions and suggest changes.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Credit comparisons that refer to both models. The justification mark must use the scenario (incomplete requirements / teacher feedback). Waterfall can only earn the recommendation mark if strongly justified from the scenario — it is not the expected answer.', null),
  ('f49783d2-c13f-5e7c-acb0-841e6ea102ba', 'c7174360-2d47-5bc9-a661-bdccd4b0ad13', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): interviews (with librarians / director); questionnaires (to readers / staff); observation of staff issuing books; examining documents (loan cards, records)', '[{"criterion":"First method","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different method","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Interviewing the librarians. 2 Examining the existing paper loan cards.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Methods must be different.', null),
  ('c3d09d87-cd1b-50ca-8225-9f6bb222cc9c', 'a5dc03ea-8069-51ad-ba55-f20b5f90af27', 1, true, '- To check whether the project is possible / worth doing (technically, economically, legally, operationally, within the schedule) (1)
- so that money and time are not wasted on a project that cannot succeed / to decide whether to go ahead (1)', '[{"criterion":"Checks whether the project is possible / worthwhile","marks":1},{"criterion":"Avoids wasting time and money / supports the decision to proceed","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It checks whether the system can be built within the library''s budget, time and legal limits, so the director does not waste money on a project that cannot succeed.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e467b040-aabe-520a-9eff-98f68ef603df', 'e2e84512-4f19-54d6-9bec-5850752da2a8', 1, true, 'C — acceptance testing (1)', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"C"}'::jsonb, null, 'Acceptance testing is done by the client before accepting the system.'),
  ('2d0a317a-e798-5bea-bcf1-be5e05443825', 'bb24b3ad-014a-5385-bb2a-5b59a3c267ab', 1, true, '- Waterfall (1)
