- security problems can be found early (1)

Max 2', '[{"criterion":"Refers to the high risk / size of the project","marks":1},{"criterion":"Spiral analyses and reduces risks in every loop","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The bank''s project is large and high-risk, and the spiral model carries out a risk analysis in every loop, so security and technical risks are found and reduced with prototypes before the whole system is built.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('bd074fce-48f4-5360-b337-01880a7cecba', 'a952cdd5-9753-5384-b524-33c40fef9a6c', 1, true, 'Analysis of models (max 4):
- Waterfall: clear structure, documentation, cost estimated (1); but inflexible, risks and errors found late — dangerous for a security-critical system (1)
- Agile: flexible, early working versions, client feedback (1); but less documentation, unpredictable cost, risk management not central — weak for strict security rules (1)
- Spiral: risk analysis every loop, prototypes reduce risk, suitable for large projects (1); but expensive, needs risk specialists, timescale uncertain (1)

Conclusion (max 2):
- Spiral is most suitable (1)
- justified by the scenario: high risk / security / large and expensive project, so the cost of risk analysis is worth it (1)

Accept another conclusion only if well justified from the scenario.', '[{"criterion":"Advantage of a first model","marks":1},{"criterion":"Disadvantage of the first model","marks":1},{"criterion":"Advantage of a second model","marks":1},{"criterion":"Disadvantage of the second model","marks":1},{"criterion":"Clear conclusion naming the most suitable model","marks":1},{"criterion":"Conclusion justified using the scenario","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Waterfall is easy to manage and well documented, but it is inflexible and testing happens late, so security problems might only be found at the end. Agile delivers working versions early and adapts to change, but it has less documentation and less control of cost and risk. The spiral model analyses risks in every loop and uses prototypes, which suits a large, high-risk system, although it is expensive and needs specialists. The spiral model is the most suitable, because the bank''s project is large, expensive and security-critical, so the extra cost of risk analysis is justified.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Analysis marks need specific advantages/disadvantages, not just names. Maximum 4 analysis marks and 2 conclusion marks. The justification must use the scenario (risk, security, size, cost).', null),
  ('d57bcbcd-47fd-5f93-a6c0-9585b5b356e6', 'cbaf1fd8-1738-542a-ab76-c6835d5fa2fb', 1, true, '- Software that manages / controls / maintains the computer (hardware) (1)
