- System software is needed for the computer to work (OS); application software is not
- System software runs in the background / starts with the computer; applications run when the user opens them
- Users interact directly with applications; little direct interaction with system software
- Applications depend on / run on top of the system software', '[{"criterion":"First valid difference","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid difference","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 System software controls the computer, while application software lets the user carry out a task. 2 The computer cannot work without system software (the OS), but it can work without applications.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Each box must state a difference, not only an example. Do not award the same idea twice.', null),
  ('5de87d73-088d-5caf-8308-b006921e3a43', 'f26f78f6-1eef-5a65-9e53-2c5973dc4ea4', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each):
