  ('71f9482f-f69c-596b-98cc-b6fbe8801ab5', '5f553c38-2aba-5f68-a5ea-a5afd61edae3', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): manages memory; manages the processor / multitasking; manages files and folders; manages input/output devices / peripherals; provides a user interface; provides a platform for applications; provides security / user accounts', '[{"criterion":"First valid purpose","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid purpose","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 It manages the memory, giving each running program its own space. 2 It provides a user interface so Aliya can open programs and files.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Purposes must be different. A bare one-word answer (e.g. ''memory'') is not enough — it must say what the OS does.', null),
