- Natural language processing analyses the words / grammar to find the meaning / intent (set alarm, 7:00)
- The device carries out the action
- It replies using speech synthesis / text-to-speech', '[{"criterion":"First valid step","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second valid step","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third valid step","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The microphone records the voice, speech recognition turns the sound into text, and natural language processing works out that the user wants an alarm at 7:00. The assistant sets the alarm and confirms it using speech synthesis.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('170817f9-02c4-5d23-a462-b9674b722966', '5fabd5ec-8ecb-55ab-ade3-91833176bb39', 1, true, 'A and C. One mark each; a mark is lost for each incorrect option selected.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":["A","C"]}'::jsonb, null, 'Background noise and accents are typical problems for NLIs.'),
  ('b78bad8c-c328-5e66-aeb7-66236e51012d', '735472dd-c8ad-585d-8238-0ad2fe9a6ec8', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): language is ambiguous / misinterpretation; struggles with colloquial language, homophones, context; accents / dialects / speech impairments; background noise; users may need to learn specific phrases; limited languages supported; privacy — always listening / recordings stored; needs processing power / Internet', '[{"criterion":"First valid disadvantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid disadvantage","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Human language is ambiguous, so the system may misunderstand the request. 2 It may not recognise the words if there is background noise or a strong accent.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('87c2b9d1-2ab7-566a-ae67-cb87fda9068c', 'e53e6a75-f5c2-5ce4-bee2-80a4e973c26a', 1, true, 'True.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":true}'::jsonb, null, 'Homophones are a source of ambiguity; the system must use context to decide which word was meant.'),
  ('2cdc3c1d-c1f4-5d26-bb64-6f0ddfba4686', '8bffcd2f-4535-5359-8606-476ac5dd5129', 1, true, '- Movements of the user''s hands / body are detected by sensors / cameras / touchscreen and interpreted as commands (1)
- Example: swipe / pinch-to-zoom on a phone; Kinect; waving to control a smart TV; VR controllers (1)', '[{"criterion":"Body movements detected and interpreted as commands","marks":1},{"criterion":"Valid example","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'An interface in which sensors such as cameras or a touchscreen detect the user''s hand or body movements and interpret them as commands, for example pinching to zoom on a phone.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('9876f7bd-c607-5e64-bf02-39e556aa79a1', '37267b38-036c-5cb4-8c67-1a929b2f3789', 1, true, 'A and C. One mark each; a mark is lost for each incorrect option selected.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":["A","C"]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('2c60ff3e-20a0-53ad-a4b2-6a82afb28031', '3446cf02-a0ac-554a-bd52-83634dfd2a33', 1, true, 'Advantage (1): natural / intuitive; touchless — hygienic; useful for people who cannot use a keyboard / mouse; immersive for games / VR; frees the hands

Disadvantage (1): gestures misinterpreted / accidental gestures; users must learn gestures; limited number of commands; tiring; expensive sensors; affected by lighting / space; less precise', '[{"criterion":"Valid advantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Valid disadvantage","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Advantage: the user can control the device without touching it. Disadvantage: an accidental movement may be read as a command.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('8470a237-f782-502d-a40e-98960d0ec0a2', 'c0062741-9e2e-5b5c-8b0e-d7def91545e8', 1, true, 'Natural language (1): ambiguous, leading to misinterpretation of user input; system may struggle with colloquial language, homophones or context; users may need to learn specific phrases; accents / background noise; privacy

Gesture recognition (1): gestures may be misinterpreted / unintended commands; users must learn the gestures; limited set of commands; tiring; needs cameras / sensors; affected by lighting', '[{"criterion":"Valid NLI disadvantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Valid GRI disadvantage","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Natural language: the system may misinterpret the user because language is ambiguous. Gesture recognition: an accidental movement may be recognised as a command.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Each box is marked separately; the disadvantage must belong to that interface.', null),
  ('cf7fd8eb-2684-521b-9772-00b3386bec90', '2cce7e4b-1993-517c-8832-6e508a957b6d', 1, true, 'Up to 4 marks:
- Both are touchless, so the screen stays clean / chefs do not need to wash hands (1)
- NLI: hands-free and no gestures to learn (1), but the noisy kitchen makes speech recognition unreliable / misinterpretation (1)
- GRI: works in a noisy kitchen (1), but gestures may be misread / need to be learnt / steam or lighting may affect the camera (1)
- Justified conclusion, e.g. gesture because of the noise (1)', '[{"criterion":"Valid point about NLI linked to the kitchen","marks":1},{"criterion":"Valid point about GRI linked to the kitchen","marks":1},{"criterion":"A drawback of one of the interfaces in this setting","marks":1},{"criterion":"Justified conclusion","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Both interfaces let chefs use the screen without touching it, so it stays clean. A natural language interface would be hands-free, but the kitchen is noisy, so the system would often misunderstand the chefs. A gesture interface is not affected by noise; the chefs could swipe in the air to change page, although they would need to learn the gestures. Gesture recognition is more suitable because of the noise.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Either choice can get full marks if justified using the scenario.', null),
  ('7d2ad930-2b24-5c7f-bcde-7b9e3eb9f86d', '4396beeb-ca3a-50fa-9d3e-2f45f60efbda', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): customers have no training / many different customers; icons / buttons are easy to recognise; no commands to remember; fewer errors as options are selected; quick to use', '[{"criterion":"First valid reason","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second valid reason","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Customers have no training, and with a GUI they just touch clearly labelled buttons instead of remembering commands, so they make fewer mistakes.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e30f85a0-44a3-54b3-b6fb-72bfa8194c84', '22b25801-bc95-576b-a40c-6458ac8fe97b', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): faster for experts; full control of the server / all settings; scripts automate tasks; uses few resources on the server; good for remote access', '[{"criterion":"First valid reason","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid reason","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 They can automate repeated tasks on many servers with scripts. 2 They have full control of all the server''s settings.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('bdbb03af-7850-5fe9-8bec-9a7e077403c0', 'fbb793c0-c7d9-5c83-a9dc-75826b14475a', 1, true, 'Problem (1) + explanation (1), e.g.
- Gestures may be misinterpreted (1) so the wrong amount / option may be selected (1)
- Customers must learn the gestures (1) so some customers could not use the machine (1)
- Lighting / weather outside affects the camera (1) so gestures are not recognised (1)
- Other people''s movements nearby may be detected (1) causing unintended commands (1)', '[{"criterion":"Valid problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation linked to the cash machine","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A gesture could be misread by the camera, so the machine might select the wrong option or amount of money.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('5942ec4c-fd6b-54d9-a37d-38ba452576ad', 'f843dd9a-7b01-54fa-a81c-5e37f19525be', 1, true, 'Evaluation points (max 5), e.g.
- GUI: intuitive icons / touch, no training (1); but not usable by visually impaired visitors (1)
- CLI: unsuitable — visitors would need to know commands / not intuitive (1)
- NLI: visitors can ask questions in speech, good for visually impaired visitors / children (1); but noise in the museum / accents / language may cause misinterpretation (1)
- GRI: touchless, hygienic, engaging (1); but gestures must be learnt / limited commands / not accessible to all (1)

Recommendation justified (1), e.g. a touch GUI combined with a natural language (voice) option for visually impaired visitors', '[{"criterion":"Evaluates GUI","marks":1},{"criterion":"Evaluates CLI","marks":1},{"criterion":"Evaluates NLI","marks":1},{"criterion":"Evaluates GRI","marks":1},{"criterion":"Further point linked to the visitors / museum","marks":1},{"criterion":"Justified recommendation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A touch-screen GUI is intuitive for visitors of all ages because they just touch icons, but visually impaired visitors cannot see the icons. A CLI is unsuitable because visitors would have to know exact commands. A natural language interface lets visitors simply ask questions aloud, which helps visually impaired people and children, although noise in the museum and different accents may cause it to misunderstand. A gesture interface is engaging and touchless, but visitors would have to learn the gestures and it would not help blind visitors. I recommend a touch GUI with a voice (natural language) option, so that every visitor can use the information point.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('f31db283-a8f8-5e47-8bdf-abce65f10751', 'e08371e3-e9e4-53eb-8db3-9d882e419b90', 1, true, '1 GUI; 2 CLI; 3 CLI; 4 GUI; 5 CLI

Five correct (3); three or four (2); one or two (1)', '[{"criterion":"One or two rows correct","marks":1},{"criterion":"Three or four rows correct","marks":1},{"criterion":"All five rows correct","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"]]}'::jsonb, 'Award 3 for five correct rows, 2 for three or four, 1 for one or two.', null),
  ('0ae9255d-526b-56cf-887d-d200b8163ed1', '51d60ac7-610e-5309-81e7-8aae58cd1e05', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): easy to learn / little training; no commands to remember; fewer errors; can see bookings visually / WYSIWYG; several windows open at once; can show room photos', '[{"criterion":"First valid advantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid advantage","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 New receptionists need little training because they click icons instead of typing commands. 2 They can have the booking and payment windows open at the same time.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('b7df6c75-9b70-5891-94b9-69e65c417a05', '544b4e3a-66c3-5309-9ae1-8d3aa220621e', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each), or one reason with explanation: faster for an expert; full control over the server settings; can write scripts to automate tasks; uses few resources so the server runs faster; suitable for remote access', '[{"criterion":"Valid reason","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second reason or explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'As an expert, the technician can work faster by typing commands, and can save them as scripts to automate tasks such as backing up the server every night.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('08702ece-70df-50d8-80c5-456dae38c8bb', '1471e831-40d7-5bd2-876e-9328bd574e58', 1, true, 'Disadvantage (1) + explanation (1), e.g.
