- Privacy (1): very sensitive patient data is needed to train / use it and could be leaked (1)
- Bias (1): trained on data from some groups, so less accurate for others (1)
- Black box (1): doctors / patients cannot see why it decided (1)', '[{"criterion":"Valid ethical problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'If the AI gives a wrong diagnosis and the patient is harmed, it is unclear who is responsible — the doctor, the hospital or the company that made the AI.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('efb07b32-fd5a-5642-a636-90a222914674', 'b4d85348-e1a2-5dac-bd10-77c1a3b75ff3', 1, true, '- AI decides the NPC''s actions / behaviour (e.g. using behaviour trees / state machines / pathfinding) (1)
