  ('32e3880e-8619-5f12-b19f-db462035f9dc', 'e462bc38-d23d-51ad-80c6-a8e6a7e63caa', 1, true, 'For each of three spheres: specific application described (1) + benefit explained (1).
Examples: industry — predictive maintenance prevents costly breakdowns; education — adaptive learning lets students learn at their own pace; medicine — image diagnosis finds disease earlier; gaming — NPC behaviour makes games realistic; society — fraud detection protects bank customers.', '[{"criterion":"First sphere: specific application","marks":1},{"criterion":"First sphere: benefit","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second sphere: specific application","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second sphere: benefit","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third sphere: specific application","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third sphere: benefit","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'In industry, AI analyses sensor data from machines to predict breakdowns, so engineers can repair them before they fail and production is not stopped. In medicine, deep-learning systems examine X-rays and MRI scans to detect diseases such as cancer, so patients are diagnosed earlier and treated sooner. In the gaming industry, AI controls non-player characters that react to the player''s actions, which makes games more realistic and challenging.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Mark the best three spheres. Vague applications such as ''AI is used in hospitals'' do not score.', null),
