  ('d74a947c-f530-574b-a252-35c817945b27', '1431dc12-8239-53fa-8e09-4350f3bbba5b', 1, true, '- Each packet has a sequence number in its header (1)
- the receiver waits for all packets (requests missing / damaged ones) and puts them in order 1, 2, 3, 4 using the sequence numbers (1)', '[{"criterion":"Sequence numbers","marks":1},{"criterion":"Reorder / request missing","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Each packet carries a sequence number, so the receiver collects all four, asks again for any missing or damaged one, and puts them back in the order 1, 2, 3, 4.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('4b813db8-52d3-58e6-afc9-7590d594975a', 'be89d467-81ef-5ce9-a329-b2a17111a184', 1, true, 'Any two, both sides (1 each): addresses only at set-up vs in every packet; one dedicated channel vs different routes; in order vs reassembled; reserved vs shared bandwidth; connection lost vs rerouted on failure; constant vs variable delay', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 In circuit switching addresses are needed only to set up the connection, whereas in packet switching every packet carries the sender and receiver addresses. 2 Circuit switching sends all data along one reserved channel in order, whereas packets can take different routes and are reassembled.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('8e994340-e8e4-519a-b84b-5cd373a5c918', 'ca849889-3f89-5892-889f-cbe95bf60467', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): picture and sound not synchronised; interruptions / video not continuous / freezing; degraded by other competing traffic; lost packets → poor quality', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Picture and sound are not synchronised. 2 The video freezes when packets are delayed by other traffic.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
