  ('c0da21cd-4be8-5e1e-a020-de71d5cc4cae', '384bd3e9-054c-5dad-9460-c2c2ca13c0f8', 1, true, 'Any three (1 each): links shared → more users / efficient use of bandwidth; rerouting around failures → reliable; no set-up time; cheaper; only lost packets resent; one network for voice and data', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1},{"criterion":"3","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Links are shared by many users, so more customers are served with the same cables. 2 If a link fails, packets are rerouted, so service continues. 3 One network carries both calls and Internet data, which is cheaper.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('0df2fda5-13ae-5174-b9df-2f46ca6ca26d', '80574c5a-58ca-58c3-a344-78e68c5e657c', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): variable delay / jitter → speech breaks up; packets out of order / lost → gaps in speech; quality drops when network congested; header overhead', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Packets are delayed by different amounts, so the speech can break up. 2 When the network is busy, packets are lost and the call quality drops.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('12af603b-82f4-5c5b-b0b3-767d107c45fc', '3603e727-ecf2-542e-8cc7-b53bd01c7bfb', 1, true, 'Packets travel across shared networks / routers owned by others (1); could be intercepted, encryption makes them unreadable (1)', '[{"criterion":"Shared network","marks":1},{"criterion":"Encryption","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Packets cross shared networks where they could be intercepted; encryption means anyone capturing them cannot understand the call.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
