  ('b45a8920-f018-5473-8631-2aaa36c70aea', 'd4393f8a-fed7-59b5-bc3b-91a0f7d82175', 1, true, '1 Mirroring (1); 2 Backup (1); 3 Mirroring (1); 4 Backup (1)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('18277090-a939-50a3-aee6-d977c6c21494', 'b4f1baca-91d3-5ced-a7cf-d5df8db745fe', 1, true, 'Up to 4 marks:
- Mirroring copies every change immediately, so the encrypted files were written to both disks (1)
- mirroring only protects against disk failure, not malware / deletion (1)
- Regular backups, at least one offline / off-site, to restore unencrypted files (1)
- Anti-virus updated / firewall / OS updates (1)
- Staff training on phishing / not opening attachments; limited user rights (1)
[Max 4]', '[{"criterion":"Explains why mirroring failed","marks":1},{"criterion":"Recommends backups (offline / off-site)","marks":1},{"criterion":"Recommends anti-virus / firewall / updates","marks":1},{"criterion":"Further justified measure","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Disk mirroring writes every change to both disks at once, so when the ransomware encrypted the files, both copies were encrypted; mirroring only protects against a disk failing. The firm should make regular backups and keep one copy offline or off-site so it can restore the original files, install and update anti-virus software and a firewall, keep the system updated, and train staff not to open suspicious attachments.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('dfa803db-3570-5644-8a8f-55230fd1805b', '17c25b31-84d9-52da-9d62-8e9cc5f98e74', 1, true, 'One mark per well-explained measure linked to the scenario (max 5), e.g.
- locked server room / UPS / fire protection (physical)
- firewall to block Internet attacks on the server
- encryption of laptops so stolen laptops do not expose data
- strong passwords + 2FA / biometrics for staff log-in, access rights so pupils cannot see marks
- anti-virus with updates against malware
- regular off-site / cloud backups to restore after loss or ransomware
- disk mirroring so the server keeps running if a disk fails
Evaluation / conclusion (1): e.g. no single measure is enough; mirroring is not a backup; cost vs risk', '[{"criterion":"First measure explained","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second measure explained","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third measure explained","marks":1},{"criterion":"Fourth measure explained","marks":1},{"criterion":"Fifth measure explained","marks":1},{"criterion":"Evaluation / conclusion","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The server should be in a locked room with a UPS, so it cannot be stolen or damaged by a power cut. A firewall should block unauthorised connections from the Internet. Teachers'' laptops should be encrypted, so if one is stolen the pupils'' data cannot be read. Staff should log in with strong passwords and two-factor authentication, and access rights should stop pupils from seeing marks. Anti-virus software must be kept updated. The server should use disk mirroring so it keeps running if a disk fails, but because mirroring copies deletions and ransomware too, the school also needs regular backups stored off-site. No single measure is enough, so the school should combine them.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('8d61512c-0639-5f37-9aa7-ce00f16b3843', 'bcd6a85c-1b14-5ff2-91da-bc5468814b70', 1, true, 'Biometric (1) Access control (1) Antivirus (1) Firewall (1) Use double authentication (1) Use strong password (1) Intranet (1) Encryption (1) [max 3] Accept any correct answer', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Firewall. 2 Strong passwords. 3 Two-factor authentication.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e6a9c8df-71b0-5348-b362-1965addb04a5', '2e08663c-d6e9-5f9c-8e6e-3d6319a4ce3e', 1, true, 'Checks / monitors packets entering and leaving the network (1); against security rules — IP addresses / ports (1); blocks unauthorised traffic (1) [Max 2]', '[{"criterion":"Checks packets against rules","marks":1},{"criterion":"Blocks unauthorised traffic","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It checks each packet coming from the Internet against security rules and blocks any connection that is not allowed.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('2abedb45-acf5-5674-8dd5-3ddafbdce359', '4673dd17-7ceb-5d96-b3e3-20d992892472', 1, true, 'Any one (1): virus on a USB stick / in an allowed e-mail attachment; insider / authorised user misusing data; phishing; physical theft; disk failure', '[{"criterion":"Valid threat","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A virus brought in on a USB stick.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
