  ('3250dad9-13c2-5407-b147-83270e7878b5', '7e3edb97-2d70-507e-aebb-2501077136c2', 1, true, 'Any four comparative points (1 each): fixed vs variable size; physical vs logical division; invisible vs visible to programmer; page table vs segment table with base and limit; internal vs external fragmentation; segmentation easier sharing / protection', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1},{"criterion":"3","marks":1},{"criterion":"4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Pages are fixed size whereas segments vary; paging splits by physical size, segmentation by logical parts such as code and data; paging uses a page table, segmentation a segment table with base and limit; paging gives internal fragmentation, segmentation external.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('66d70516-9900-5ee8-a531-7c518cce2cbf', '68a7abb1-00f6-5e2a-8251-68cb8359b716', 1, true, 'Software that emulates a computer (1); guest OS / program runs as if on own hardware while sharing host (1)', '[{"criterion":"Emulates computer","marks":1},{"criterion":"Guest on host","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Software that emulates a whole computer, so a guest OS runs on it as if on real hardware while using the host''s resources.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('06606355-133b-5860-b72c-e6201b38c45a', '4c29e06e-8772-5363-b35b-e2656f8c200a', 1, true, 'Java compiled to platform-independent bytecode (1); JVM on each OS translates / interprets bytecode for that machine (1)', '[{"criterion":"Bytecode","marks":1},{"criterion":"JVM per platform","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Java is compiled to bytecode, which is the same on every platform; each OS has its own JVM that translates the bytecode into that computer''s machine code.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('61cef731-ae9f-5143-b89a-9c2570933901', 'ce9aa4a0-daec-579a-af70-66f93a35eb06', 1, true, 'Up to 2 advantages (1 each): one computer runs all three OSs — cheaper / less space; isolation — crashes do not harm host; snapshots to restore a clean state; easy to copy / share setups. Up to 2 disadvantages (1 each): slower — performance results may not match real hardware; needs much RAM / CPU / storage; hardware access limited; OS licences; host failure stops all', '[{"criterion":"Adv 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Adv 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Dis 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Dis 2","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'One powerful computer can run all three systems, saving money, and snapshots let testers reset after a crash. However, the VMs run slower so timing tests may be unrealistic, and the host needs a lot of RAM and storage.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('0489a311-c32b-5b92-b75b-74d3d76245a3', '33fb4f2f-de4e-5e15-a1d9-3bf43704f36a', 1, true, '- Gaining unauthorised access to a computer system / network / data (1)
- usually with malicious intent, e.g. to steal, change or damage data (1)', '[{"criterion":"Unauthorised access","marks":1},{"criterion":"Malicious intent / purpose","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Breaking into a computer system or its data without permission, usually to steal, change or damage information.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('3f6e80d4-51c7-5f08-a077-96043ee70893', '80bfcd10-0b85-5658-99e4-9a876f2083c6', 1, true, 'Black–R1, White–R2, Grey–R3. One mark per correct match.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3"}}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('5c73a075-e4b5-58c7-98f5-1a17655cdb0c', '2a362f78-3621-5dc5-9f4d-a4b9674dae11', 1, true, 'L1–R1, L2–R2, L3–R3, L4–R4. One mark per correct match.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4"}}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('53a86520-368f-53fd-b2ce-bde7d7347a6a', 'a45cecba-a23e-5987-b265-f5fd1fc51d1a', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): customers'' privacy is violated; identity theft; theft of money / card details; innocent customers harmed; loss of trust; confidential business data stolen; blackmail', '[{"criterion":"First problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second problem","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Customers'' private details are exposed, violating their privacy. 2 Stolen card details may be used to take customers'' money.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('c521b757-67a3-520d-960c-4f8793fc0a9b', '01ebae71-6b73-59ca-be00-2b2e8b5e5d5f', 1, true, 'Any three developed points (1 each): patients'' confidential medical data exposed — privacy violated / discrimination / blackmail; records may be changed — wrong treatment endangers lives; systems unavailable — treatment delayed; hospital fined / loses reputation / patients lose trust; cost of recovery and security improvements', '[{"criterion":"First developed point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second developed point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third developed point","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Patients'' medical histories could be published or sold, violating their privacy and possibly leading to blackmail or discrimination. If the attacker changes records, patients could receive the wrong medicine, which could endanger lives. The hospital may also be fined for failing to protect personal data and patients may stop trusting it.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e0342d06-810b-58ea-ac3b-1788fff8c502', 'd6fd98ce-5bd7-5b72-98d9-503b295bccbf', 1, true, 'False.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":false}'::jsonb, null, 'Unauthorised access is itself an offence, whether or not data is changed.'),
  ('c84e1c7f-eac4-5085-8a6c-b21b0e4e0e86', '6e06783a-a0c6-5918-afde-01af516d9659', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): enacting two-factor authentication; increasing password complexity; using SSL protocol; encrypting; hashing; limiting login attempts; firewall; access rights; updates
[max 2]', '[{"criterion":"First way","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second way","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Use two-factor authentication. 2 Limit the number of login attempts.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e02829e6-d8c1-5b4a-9c40-fe63fff4da16', '5b1c9a1b-bdfe-5c5a-a8c2-dd4cb1c2f900', 1, true, '- A brute-force attack tries very many passwords one after another (1)
- after a few wrong attempts the account is locked / delayed, so the attacker cannot try enough passwords (1)', '[{"criterion":"Brute force = many guesses","marks":1},{"criterion":"Lock-out stops further guesses","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A brute-force program tries thousands of passwords; if the account is locked after, say, five wrong attempts, the program cannot keep guessing until it finds the right one.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('3816215d-6235-57cf-a6e2-ce58fe712dec', '9bce53e3-e8fc-5ea4-9714-9a37489e25c9', 1, true, 'C', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"C"}'::jsonb, null, 'It is long and mixes upper and lower case letters, digits and symbols, and is not a word or name.'),
  ('35568bbb-8c06-5dbc-922b-33a81744affb', '0eb90912-78c5-59b1-8359-0027363dbc15', 1, true, '1 Authentication (1); 2 Authorisation (1); 3 Authentication (1); 4 Authorisation (1)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('fb32f7d3-b5c4-5c25-af24-c98423161a03', 'c21be83b-6f41-5bf9-8619-e7b0e6f06f2b', 1, true, 'Any two from: encrypting data (1); granting limited access rights (1); blocking access from certain locations (1); keeping logs of user entries (1); 2FA; firewall; physical security', '[{"criterion":"First measure","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second measure","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Encrypt the data. 2 Give each employee access only to the data they need.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e57a1d61-c1ad-5982-a785-95ece32a8dc5', '7b992535-3e87-55d4-9469-120079cea55d', 1, true, '- A hash is a one-way transformation — the password cannot be worked out from it (1)
- so if the database is stolen, the attacker does not get the users'' actual passwords (1)', '[{"criterion":"One-way","marks":1},{"criterion":"Stolen database does not reveal passwords","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Hashing is one-way, so the original password cannot be recovered from the hash; if crackers steal the database, they still do not have users'' passwords.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('2e30a5ad-e20f-5e62-a0dc-8c411a83e58b', 'bc218a22-a261-5a73-86a9-c798ed88372f', 1, true, 'L1–R1, L2–R2, L3–R3, L4–R4. One mark per correct match.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4"}}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('d868d091-8dec-589f-893e-522de591e780', '479a509e-fe60-5f09-9b20-2f66d5f855dc', 1, true, '- A virus attaches to a host file / program and spreads when that file is run or shared (needs user action) (1)
- A worm is a standalone program that copies itself across networks automatically (1)', '[{"criterion":"Virus needs host / user action","marks":1},{"criterion":"Worm spreads by itself","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A virus needs a host file and spreads when a user runs or shares that file, whereas a worm is a separate program that spreads across networks on its own.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('a3962e13-deb4-526c-b8d1-f408147caa40', '365451c8-39ce-598a-805d-706f3fdee5a4', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): files cannot be opened / data loss; work stops — downtime / lost income; ransom payment / cost of recovery; customers'' data leaked / fines; reputation damage; no guarantee files are returned after paying', '[{"criterion":"First problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second problem","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Staff cannot open any files, so the company cannot work. 2 The company may lose money paying the ransom or restoring its systems.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('973d4031-78a5-55f4-acc8-1a7f166492b6', '86eaf65c-13ac-5e06-954f-96a8ba495029', 1, true, 'True.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":true}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('067563b6-fb21-54f7-a2bc-74c7fe708178', 'dcf474cf-0e6c-5fb1-833d-5f5fdd6b9f4a', 1, true, '- It tells users what personal data is collected and how it is used / stored / shared (1)
- so users can give informed consent / know their rights; it is required by law (1)', '[{"criterion":"Explains data collection and use","marks":1},{"criterion":"Informed consent / rights / law","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It explains what personal data the website collects and how it is used, stored and shared, so users can decide whether to agree and know what rights they have.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('d81729a8-bde5-582a-b9db-72d635d605a8', '432808dc-9d2a-52f2-9b4c-ddcbd0005471', 1, true, 'A and C. One mark each; a mark is lost for each incorrect option selected.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":["A","C"]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('7631ddf4-2928-560d-9665-d6c33fca6720', '82ab5e83-0917-5c85-a3c2-1e3850e390c5', 1, true, 'Data: heart rate and location (1)
Shared with: research partners (anonymised) (1)
Right: download / delete their data (1)', '[{"criterion":"Heart rate and location","marks":1},{"criterion":"Research partners","marks":1},{"criterion":"Download / delete","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Heart rate and location; anonymised data with research partners; the user can delete their data.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('07a71249-a4bc-522d-9fc8-64e9cbad15ef', '9802a55b-c45e-54e5-8b0e-b731c324b944', 1, true, 'Problems (max 3): patient records unavailable — treatments / operations delayed, lives at risk; appointments cancelled / patients sent elsewhere; cost of ransom or recovery; data may also be stolen and leaked — privacy; reputation / trust; paying does not guarantee recovery and funds criminals
Prevention (max 2): regular offline / off-site backups; anti-virus and updates; staff training on phishing; network segmentation / firewall; limited access rights
[Max 4]', '[{"criterion":"First problem analysed","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second problem analysed","marks":1},{"criterion":"Prevention measure","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second problem or measure developed","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Doctors cannot open patients'' records, so operations are delayed and lives may be at risk. The hospital loses money either paying the ransom, which does not guarantee the files are returned, or restoring its systems, and patients may lose trust in it. If it had kept regular offline backups, it could have restored the files without paying, and updated anti-virus software and staff training against phishing e-mails would have made the infection less likely.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('3aee8aff-ec0e-5020-a4f0-92a0dfa16765', 'ba2b0a87-8132-5129-80f3-23925c5ff38d', 1, true, 'Contents (max 3): data collected; purpose; sharing with third parties / advertisers; storage period and location; security measures; user rights (access, correct, delete, withdraw consent); cookies; contact; changes
Evaluation (max 3): positive — legal requirement / accountability / informed consent / trust; negative — too long / legal language, users do not read them; must accept to use the service; policies change; does not guarantee actual security; data may still be hacked
A reasoned conclusion may gain credit within the maximum.', '[{"criterion":"First content item explained","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second content item","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third content item","marks":1},{"criterion":"Positive evaluation point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Negative evaluation point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Further evaluation / conclusion","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The policy should state which personal data the network collects (profile, messages, location), why it collects it, whether it is shared with advertisers, how long it is kept and where it is stored, how it is protected, and the users'' rights to see, correct and delete their data. Policies are useful because the law requires them and they make the company accountable, so users can give informed consent. However, most people never read them because they are long and full of legal terms, users must accept them to use the service, and the company can change them. A policy also does not prevent the data from being hacked, so it protects users only partly; strong security measures and enforcement by the law are also needed.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('808abc84-a93d-5a8c-8c47-c06e303df2f1', '1d21dddf-5511-543f-bb5c-99b1f30d4440', 1, true, 'Enacting two-factor authentication (1) Increasing password complexity (1) Use SSL protocol (1) Encrypting (1) Hashing (1) Limiting login attempts (1) [max 2]', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Two-factor authentication. 2 Encrypting the data.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('39045b90-110b-5b06-abad-e4bc21d01438', 'cd119773-77b8-510b-8a74-b2f5e379b034', 1, true, '- A program tries every possible password / combination until the correct one is found (1)
- prevention: limit login attempts / lock account / long complex passwords / 2FA / CAPTCHA (1)', '[{"criterion":"Description","marks":1},{"criterion":"Prevention","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A program automatically tries every possible password until it finds the right one; locking the account after five wrong attempts prevents it.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('a8d655c5-febd-59f9-82a0-ac4100b3384f', '934bd8c7-4a2a-544d-aeff-137af26ae0f7', 1, true, 'Problem (1) + analysis (1), e.g. marks no longer reflect real work — unfair to other pupils / universities misled; other pupils'' private data accessed — privacy violated; trust in the school system lost', '[{"criterion":"Problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"Analysis","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Changed marks would be unfair to pupils who earned their marks honestly, and universities would receive false information, so the whole assessment system could no longer be trusted.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('29239b20-91ba-545e-893c-dec4dfb12f27', '50c83a83-1370-50d8-a8c7-2a95259c57b3', 1, true, '- A white-hat hacker tests the system with the owner''s permission to find and report weaknesses (1)
- a black-hat hacker breaks in illegally to steal or cause harm (1)', '[{"criterion":"White hat","marks":1},{"criterion":"Black hat","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The white-hat hacker has the school''s permission and reports the weaknesses so they can be fixed, whereas a black-hat hacker breaks in illegally to steal data or cause damage.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('679f2992-9a76-5ec0-9344-be64ece3df52', 'd8eb5757-85e6-57b5-97f8-40485f15a4be', 1, true, 'Any two from: encrypting data (1); granting limited access rights (1); blocking access from certain locations (1); keeping logs of user entries to the system (1)', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Encrypting the data. 2 Keeping logs of who opens which files.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('1606788d-6bf7-53db-bd43-44e342ed171e', '2a5cca71-5a01-55ea-ab97-5648914d8c0d', 1, true, '- Authentication checks who the user is (password, biometrics) (1)
- Authorisation decides what the user is allowed to access / do (access rights) (1)', '[{"criterion":"Authentication","marks":1},{"criterion":"Authorisation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Authentication checks the identity of the user, for example with a password; authorisation then decides which files that user may read or change.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('f9ffcd32-6dd8-5446-a120-c93dead7430a', '0c86d694-f02f-57e7-a6b9-6f7674b58d90', 1, true, '- Fewer people can see / change confidential data, so insider misuse or mistakes are less likely (1)
- if an account is cracked, the attacker can reach only a small part of the data (1)', '[{"criterion":"Reduces insider risk","marks":1},{"criterion":"Limits damage from a cracked account","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Fewer employees can see confidential data, so it is less likely to be leaked, and if one account is cracked the attacker can only reach the files that employee was allowed to use.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('6b1f3e05-3d3c-5c0b-a761-c0f6916548e0', 'da1203e8-a053-58f6-bc85-a3ffd3f8a0bc', 1, true, 'Any one (1): fine under personal data protection law; legal action / compensation claims by customers; investigation by authorities', '[{"criterion":"Valid consequence","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It could be fined under the law on personal data protection.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('dc586067-0327-5a49-ae19-29acd99a3292', '2aa61522-0ed6-50fb-bf77-18d4af52c18d', 1, true, 'L1–R1, L2–R2, L3–R3, L4–R4. One mark per correct line.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4"}}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('c92df125-4c71-5e3a-ae1a-9aed1d58d090', 'b22c52ec-b6b2-596d-bb42-f6f3fdd9f917', 1, true, 'Any four developed points (1 each): bookings / check-in impossible — flights delayed or cancelled; passengers stranded / miss connections; airline loses income / pays compensation; cost of ransom or recovery, no guarantee of recovery; passengers'' personal / payment data may be stolen — privacy, identity theft; reputation damage / loss of trust
[Max 4]', '[{"criterion":"First problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"Fourth problem / developed analysis","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Staff cannot check passengers in or sell tickets, so flights are delayed or cancelled and passengers are stranded. The airline loses income and must pay compensation, as well as the cost of restoring its systems or paying the ransom, which may not even return the data. Passengers'' personal and card details may also have been stolen, putting them at risk of fraud, and the airline''s reputation suffers.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('c47175cd-9dbd-5095-b0dd-b8d4d1f4fe53', 'f2af2fbe-1643-512c-adad-66b0efec55a0', 1, true, '- Informs users what personal data is collected and how it is used / stored / shared (1)
- so they can give informed consent / know their rights / required by law (1)', '[{"criterion":"Explains data use","marks":1},{"criterion":"Consent / rights / law","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It tells users which personal data is collected and how it is used and shared, so they can decide whether to agree and know their rights.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('a7cabeba-d2b3-5814-ba23-e06f6e5fe206', '86b508c4-462b-5e64-9aa2-031a7f096f2f', 1, true, 'Purpose: to personalise lessons (1)
Shared: e-mail address with the newsletter partner (1)
Kept: three years after the last login (1)', '[{"criterion":"Purpose","marks":1},{"criterion":"Sharing","marks":1},{"criterion":"Storage period","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'To personalise lessons; the e-mail address is shared with a newsletter partner; three years after the last login.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('3bea5d11-ac9f-5d28-a058-e072c693f600', 'f23337d7-f8e3-526a-9055-e308503abc85', 1, true, 'Reason (1) + explanation (1): users do not read long / legal policies so agree without understanding; must accept to use the service; company can change the policy; policy does not stop data being hacked / partner may misuse data', '[{"criterion":"Valid reason","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Most users do not read long policies written in legal language, so they agree to their e-mail being shared without realising it.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('10ac2880-f745-535c-a742-85ce46858273', '55bb68c7-a7b1-5bfb-8bae-4f91327084e8', 1, true, '- Creations of the mind (non-physical) that the creator owns and has legal rights over (1)
- Example: software, a song, a book, a film, an invention, a logo / brand name (1)', '[{"criterion":"Definition","marks":1},{"criterion":"Example","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Creations of the mind, such as software or music, that belong to their creator, who has the legal right to control how they are used.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('060f001a-4e72-5a5a-984a-dc2c50e942a5', '0c8a75d3-1de5-5717-af61-58c5de276e49', 1, true, 'Source code → Copyright (1); Solar panel → Patent (1); Logo → Trademark (1); Novel → Copyright (1)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓","",""],[null,"","✓",""],[null,"","","✓"],[null,"✓","",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('738eee62-69f0-5bb8-bb61-cd6a60840124', '1acca781-0dca-562f-8bff-bf25f975c9a2', 1, true, '- Copyright protects original works (code, text, music) and is automatic (1)
- A patent protects an invention / technical solution and must be applied for and registered (1)', '[{"criterion":"Copyright","marks":1},{"criterion":"Patent","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Copyright protects original works such as program code and arises automatically, whereas a patent protects an invention and must be registered.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('d1d4a3b7-6f21-525d-8f62-dbd97c3dd6f1', '4c34ab3b-9be6-561a-b070-24750168ac1e', 1, true, 'False.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":false}'::jsonb, null, 'Copyright applies automatically; the photo can only be used with permission or under its licence.'),
  ('ef238de5-dbbd-5d57-b1fd-4b66dc1944f0', '0d9b4de7-8d02-5af1-b8d2-74333f8c4085', 1, true, 'L1–R1, L2–R2, L3–R3, L4–R4. One mark per correct match.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4"}}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e76805ca-5566-50c7-982d-76cf6ac2c9c0', '28dab1c1-9694-5b1c-8788-fcb8ce2cb973', 1, true, 'Any three developed points (1 each): developers lose income / royalties; less money for new games / jobs; users break the law — fines; pirated copies may contain malware; no updates / support / online play; lost tax revenue; unethical — using work without paying', '[{"criterion":"First point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third point","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The game company loses income, so it has less money to pay developers and make new games. People who download pirated copies break copyright law and may be fined, and the copies often contain malware that can steal their data.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('d8fbbc35-1766-5643-bc78-d7aaea1dcb89', 'df2a1809-a9ff-55dd-b7a1-2178f46f394c', 1, true, '- Presenting someone else''s work / ideas as your own without acknowledging the source (1)
- Avoid by citing sources / using quotation marks / paraphrasing in your own words with a reference / a bibliography (1)', '[{"criterion":"Definition","marks":1},{"criterion":"How to avoid","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Plagiarism is presenting another person''s work as your own. A student avoids it by putting quotations in quotation marks and citing every source in a reference list.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('80c63f2f-a233-5a8b-9ea0-3fa14d9631ca', '406a898b-47ed-55fe-90dc-043db6882bf0', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): ask the owner for permission; use Creative Commons / copyright-free images and follow the licence; credit / attribute the author; buy a licence (stock photo); create their own image', '[{"criterion":"First way","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second way","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Use an image with a Creative Commons licence and credit the author. 2 Ask the photographer for permission.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('25d346fa-028b-58fd-83e1-fdc4665deef7', '03675172-aa9d-5539-a135-38ba4561bcc1', 1, true, 'B', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"B"}'::jsonb, null, 'BY = give credit to the author; NC = non-commercial use only.'),
  ('5b680971-526f-5b23-9fa5-200cda67d2ad', '7f9d72ed-c86a-5c3a-9939-5042afaa30a6', 1, true, 'Any three developed points (1 each): people may take a harmful treatment / avoid a safe one — health risk; spreads faster than corrections; panic / shortages; damages the reputation of doctors / companies; loss of trust in reliable sources; difficult to remove once shared', '[{"criterion":"First point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third point","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'People may stop taking a safe medicine or take a dangerous one, putting their health at risk. False posts spread much faster than corrections, so many people see them, and trust in doctors and reliable news sources falls.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('be826bce-deda-5314-b3c0-b902dcd0acdd', '101e614b-551b-588e-9721-f1f85b3daf30', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): check the author / source is known and reliable; compare with other reliable sources; check the date; use fact-checking websites; check the website address / domain; look for evidence / references', '[{"criterion":"First way","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second way","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Compare it with other reliable sources. 2 Check who the author is and when it was published.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('d6b07dbf-2f50-5ba5-9fdd-fab044318834', '83c3ebd7-bad7-5dd8-9c9a-f69d4ac5480a', 1, true, 'A and C. One mark each; a mark is lost for each incorrect option selected.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":["A","C"]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('30f6333f-eb05-591b-86e3-a187f0eb4569', '22beaee3-de87-5cc6-9f07-892b94e28767', 1, true, '- Providing public / state services to citizens and businesses online using the Internet (1)
- egov.kz / eGov mobile (1)', '[{"criterion":"Definition","marks":1},{"criterion":"egov.kz","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The use of the Internet by the state to provide public services online; in Kazakhstan the portal is egov.kz.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('882edff0-85d8-5a7b-9682-859e690983a4', '5e46f4a8-dc00-5f5c-98e2-e5ae0149aeaa', 1, true, 'Any three (1 each): certificates (address, no criminal record, birth / marriage); registration of residence / car / business; paying taxes / fines; applying to kindergarten / school; booking a doctor / attaching to a clinic; social benefits / pension information; digital documents; licences (elicense.kz)', '[{"criterion":"First service","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second service","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third service","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Getting a certificate of address registration. 2 Paying a traffic fine. 3 Applying for a place in a kindergarten.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('1578085d-0f51-5115-81d7-1d8a51cd32da', 'ef4e6d36-4589-5636-8587-28e52dedca87', 1, true, '- Confirms / proves the identity of the person signing (authentication) (1)
- shows that the document has not been changed after signing / has legal force like a handwritten signature (1)', '[{"criterion":"Proves identity","marks":1},{"criterion":"Integrity / legal force","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It proves that the application was signed by the citizen and not someone else, and shows that the document has not been changed after it was signed.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('247b1a9d-2346-5345-aeac-8b38cd501fae', '15fc2251-6ef3-5756-9c57-caf24579ec8e', 1, true, '1 Advantage (1); 2 Risk (1); 3 Advantage (1); 4 Risk (1)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('7b6eb1aa-6505-5a8e-830e-c05184ed8ebc', '45f0f3f5-538d-5330-99b4-11a9657a8344', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): never share EDS password / SMS code; type egov.kz or use the official app — do not follow links in messages; check HTTPS and the address; log out on shared computers; keep the EDS file on a protected device', '[{"criterion":"First precaution","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second precaution","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Never tell anyone the SMS code. 2 Type egov.kz into the browser instead of clicking links in messages.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('66958747-5aed-5d00-8bf0-6ce31958221b', '210920f0-b37b-5997-bbe5-3737719dc7a6', 1, true, 'Problems (max 2): copyright infringement for the song / photos — video removed / blocked, disqualification, fines; copied text is plagiarism; creators lose income / credit
Solutions (max 2): royalty-free / Creative Commons music; CC or own photos with attribution / permission; rewrite text in own words and cite the website; check licence conditions (non-commercial)
[Max 4]', '[{"criterion":"First problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"First solution","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second solution","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The song and photos are protected by copyright, so YouTube may block the video and the students could be disqualified or fined; copying text from the travel site is plagiarism. They should use royalty-free or Creative Commons music, take their own photos or use CC photos with credit to the authors, and write the text in their own words, citing the website.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('2ebfc378-a2e7-5938-ab81-8a34fe37b9ab', 'ac59ab54-75f0-5786-9a51-5e5c38e74769', 1, true, 'Services (max 2): specific examples with benefit
Advantages (max 2): 24/7, saves time and travel, less paperwork, less corruption, transparency, automatic data from state databases
Security (max 1): EDS, SMS codes, biometrics
Problems (max 2): digital divide, cyber-attacks / data leaks, phishing, technical failures
Conclusion (1)
[Max 6]', '[{"criterion":"Specific service with benefit","marks":1},{"criterion":"Advantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Security measure explained","marks":1},{"criterion":"Problem explained","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second problem / advantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Reasoned conclusion","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'On egov.kz citizens can get certificates, pay fines and apply to kindergartens online at any time, which saves queues and travel, especially for people far from offices. Fewer face-to-face contacts with officials also reduce corruption. Applications are signed with an electronic digital signature or a one-time SMS code, which confirms the citizen''s identity. However, elderly people or those without Internet access may be unable to use the services, and fake eGov sites and messages are used to steal codes. A large state database is also a target for hackers. Overall e-government is very beneficial, provided citizens are taught to use it safely and offline help remains for those who need it.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('db69791b-28ab-5b19-8015-7d62d8f2df32', '80ee00c0-e682-5c87-92d3-d482b8ec2f1f', 1, true, 'Code → Copyright (1); Logo → Trademark (1); Device → Patent (1)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓","",""],[null,"","","✓"],[null,"","✓",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('53f0f8cf-4ef2-5ce8-9dd4-2e549d473e2d', 'fce23797-beb3-5f82-8cf0-45401bb7b4d0', 1, true, 'Any three developed points (1 each): company loses income; less investment in updates / jobs; users of cracked copies break the law; cracked copies may contain malware / steal location data; no updates / support; damage to reputation if malware is blamed on the app', '[{"criterion":"First point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second point","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third point","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The company loses sales, so it has less money to improve the app and pay its programmers. Users of the cracked copies break copyright law, and the copies may contain malware that steals their location and personal data.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('c3ca997e-7601-5197-a665-9680572eec83', '21af49a4-0ec7-52d7-8c22-42084f5fbee6', 1, true, '- Open source: the source code is available and can be studied / modified / redistributed under the licence (1)
- Freeware: free to use but the source code is not available / cannot be modified (1)', '[{"criterion":"Open source","marks":1},{"criterion":"Freeware","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Open-source software provides its source code, which can be modified and shared under the licence, whereas freeware is free to use but its code is closed and cannot be changed.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('f3dde827-cefb-5d3c-92cf-9d523c8833ca', '7549cc90-ecf6-5bbb-a2d9-05c6e06769d2', 1, true, '- Presenting others'' work as one''s own without acknowledgement (1)
- cite sources / quotation marks / paraphrase with references (1)', '[{"criterion":"Definition","marks":1},{"criterion":"Avoidance","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Plagiarism is using someone else''s work as if it were yours. The students should write in their own words and cite every source they use.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('6cde168c-06af-5849-97c3-8569172767cb', 'b4438c5d-c58d-5db5-a3a8-565409848a85', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): Creative Commons / copyright-free images following the licence; credit the author; ask permission; buy a licence', '[{"criterion":"First way","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second way","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Use Creative Commons photos. 2 Credit the photographer.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('4f65b84c-9850-5b2e-b4ce-6fb1e0ab3b26', '0fd46755-c8f9-5983-9b03-f78fd23476ec', 1, true, 'Problems (max 2): people make wrong decisions / ignore real risks; spreads faster than corrections; reduces trust in scientists / media; influences policy / votes
Checking (max 2): author / organisation reliable; compare with scientific sources; check date and evidence / references; fact-checking sites; check the domain', '[{"criterion":"First problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second problem","marks":1},{"criterion":"First check","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second check","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'People who believe the video may ignore real dangers and oppose useful measures, and because false videos spread faster than corrections, trust in scientists falls. The students should check who made the video and compare its claims with reliable scientific sources and fact-checking sites.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('efbfa1e3-3c14-5f45-afa1-c79be93872aa', '61f58986-153c-5d79-a851-d90785f6e67c', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): pay taxes / fines; register a car / business / residence; apply to a school / kindergarten; book a doctor; social payments / pension; digital documents; licences', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Paying a traffic fine. 2 Registering a car.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('77e88b4f-b8ed-570d-80f1-83a3c6f87c6b', 'fb7d2c03-6ecf-5bd1-ba21-b45db9555258', 1, true, '- Confirms his identity (1)
- shows the request has not been altered / gives it legal force (1)', '[{"criterion":"Identity","marks":1},{"criterion":"Integrity / legal force","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It proves that the request comes from Mr Seitkali and that it has not been changed after he signed it.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('661ed22f-6f9c-5d88-b0d9-2721e18eb862', '61e4e77e-17cc-5f15-aaf2-3106004ab22d', 1, true, 'Advantage (1) + explanation (1): available 24/7; no travel / queue — saves time; certificate arrives instantly as PDF with QR code; less corruption', '[{"criterion":"Advantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'He does not need to travel or wait in a queue, because the certificate appears in his personal account within minutes, at any time of day.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('3458fc2c-f5c7-5fc4-ab36-59d7b3600039', '90e5df60-c596-5d24-b632-dd852a81a4eb', 1, true, '- Phishing — a fake site to steal his code / password / EDS and access his account (1)
- He should not click the link / not share the code; go to egov.kz directly / contact the official support (1)', '[{"criterion":"Phishing risk","marks":1},{"criterion":"Correct action","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It is probably phishing: the link leads to a fake site that steals his code. He should not click it and should log in only by typing egov.kz himself.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('03b0ec45-c7a9-5be8-b6cc-b9e0f485570e', 'e5e7f54e-c410-5a7e-92d8-f63dc9154d6b', 1, true, 'Direct, parallel, pilot, phased. All four (2); two or three (1)', '[{"criterion":"Two or three methods","marks":1},{"criterion":"All four","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Direct, parallel, pilot, phased.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('37d277bf-dcc5-5eee-a366-14f462bc51c2', 'e1b96b13-fc47-554d-ac86-914e0db95dfc', 1, true, 'L1–R1, L2–R2, L3–R3, L4–R4. One mark per correct match.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4"}}'::jsonb, null, null)
