  ('f8472838-0511-5b1b-82e4-94fc1e10b384', '5bf55758-59ff-51ea-98d6-f97fd051b777', 1, true, 'One mark each (max 6): justified method (e.g. pilot in one grade / parallel); hardware / software installation and accounts; data conversion of student lists + verification; training method and timing for teachers; tasks in a sensible order with responsible people / dates; testing before go-live; contingency (keep paper registers / backup); review / support', '[{"criterion":"Method","marks":1},{"criterion":"Installation","marks":1},{"criterion":"Data conversion","marks":1},{"criterion":"Training","marks":1},{"criterion":"Order and responsibilities","marks":1},{"criterion":"Contingency","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Method: pilot in Grade 7 for two weeks, then the whole school. 1 IT technician sets up the server and accounts for 60 teachers (week 1). 2 Office staff import the class lists from the existing spreadsheet and check them against the paper registers (week 1–2). 3 Teachers attend a one-hour training session and receive a quick guide (week 2). 4 Acceptance test with test data (week 2). 5 Pilot in Grade 7 while paper registers are kept (weeks 3–4). 6 Whole-school go-live (week 5). Contingency: paper registers are kept for one term and the database is backed up every night. A review meeting is held after one month.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('d99946b5-12d7-5b32-8815-8a14cd94a462', 'dad96643-5833-5551-a462-ceb701901444', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): tasks in order / none forgotten; on time; responsibilities; risks reduced / contingency; minimal disruption; budget', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It makes sure every task is done in the correct order by the right person, so the clinic can keep treating patients during the changeover and data is not lost.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
