- and its users / accounts / security, usually running on a server (1)', '[{"criterion":"Manages network resources","marks":1},{"criterion":"Users / server","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'An OS, usually on a server, that manages the users of a network and the resources they share, such as files and printers.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('ddd4e489-3d8e-55c9-8b08-0ee241d48e6d', '0d841a2b-a745-5f39-8075-2339e8f72485', 1, true, 'NOS provides user authentication and authorization mechanisms… (1) … ensuring that only authorized users can access network resources. (1) NOS verifies user identities… (1) … to assign appropriate access rights. (1) [Max 2]', '[{"criterion":"Authentication / verification","marks":1},{"criterion":"Authorisation / access rights","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The NOS verifies each user''s identity at log-in and then gives them the access rights of their account and groups, so only authorised users can use each resource.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
