  ('ec0179cf-af4e-58f8-a2f6-247a5b55b083', '3d0d813a-63c9-5221-b2fa-e4f9604f6c50', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): centralised vs each computer manages itself; strong central security vs weaker; central backup vs individual; needs server / admin vs cheap; large vs small networks', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Client–server has central control of accounts and security on the server, whereas in peer-to-peer each computer manages itself. 2 Client–server backs up data centrally, whereas peer-to-peer users back up their own files.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('f0e018e9-9be0-5798-950b-d5f0ae535104', 'fb2a7108-fc4d-595c-8c03-dd059d47a9ca', 1, true, 'True.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":true}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('39043d9f-26cc-56ca-a378-d68a6695a74b', 'a1648a14-dd0f-5675-b983-49d879962ebf', 1, true, 'Jobs with similar requirements are batched together and run through the computer as a group (1); data is collected for a defined period of time and processed as a pack of similar tasks (1); sorting is performed before processing (1); no user interaction (1) [Max 2]', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Jobs with similar requirements are grouped and run together. 2 Data is collected over a period and processed without user interaction.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('cd71ee52-8e94-5bac-842c-0ad9c2482b03', '80c8871c-a6e3-54dc-801c-567bfc4b7630', 1, true, '(1) queue (2) sorted (3) spooling', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"blanks":[["queue"],["sorted"],["spooling","spooled"]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e8d5cced-6021-53c9-ba4c-b38d577cf2f7', '5f84270e-931b-575e-b119-dd3639767821', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): large number of similar jobs; readings collected over the quarter and processed together; not needed immediately; runs automatically at night / off-peak without operator', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'All 300 000 bills are similar calculations made only once a quarter, so the meter readings can be collected and processed together automatically overnight.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('93e3a730-6e19-508b-a8fa-8a3ebf3c8e95', '4086ad74-ae6a-5a78-a1a0-4a9e00dac220', 1, true, 'Disadvantage (1) + explanation (1): delay — results not immediate / data out of date; errors found only after the batch runs — whole batch repeated; no interaction — jobs cannot be changed', '[{"criterion":"Disadvantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Results are not immediate: a customer''s payment made today only appears after the overnight batch has run.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('4976ad50-1b7f-5803-8fe4-8f11a9b2bfe4', '86339a72-9d55-5d9b-bd7b-34ab4298355b', 1, true, 'Card payments batch (1); pacemaker real-time (1); office network (1); traffic lights real-time (1)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"","","✓"],[null,"✓","",""],[null,"","✓",""],[null,"✓","",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('6707e8aa-a17e-5ff5-90a2-b2e866c7c6be', '0bde285a-063f-59b9-9821-f5fe40242579', 1, true, 'RTOS (max 2): guaranteed deadline / deterministic / priority; suits monitors because alarms must be immediate
NOS (max 2): manages users, access rights, shared records; suits servers because many staff share data securely
Batch (max 2): groups similar jobs, no interaction, scheduled; suits monthly bills — large volume, not urgent
Comparison points credited within each', '[{"criterion":"RTOS described","marks":1},{"criterion":"RTOS suitability","marks":1},{"criterion":"NOS described","marks":1},{"criterion":"NOS suitability","marks":1},{"criterion":"Batch described","marks":1},{"criterion":"Batch suitability","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The real-time OS responds to sensor readings within a guaranteed deadline and gives the alarm task the highest priority, which suits patient monitors because a dangerous heart rate must trigger an alarm immediately. The network OS manages user accounts, authentication and access rights to shared files on the servers, so hundreds of staff can securely open the patient records they are allowed to see. The batch OS groups the month''s treatments and runs the billing jobs automatically overnight without interaction, which suits billing because there are many similar bills and they are not urgent. Unlike the RTOS, the batch OS does not respond immediately, and unlike the NOS it has no interactive users while running.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('c943e4dd-0fd0-5548-90e8-7b76418b1d22', '207fd7c4-a5cc-51cf-af44-f4e14ae88536', 1, true, 'Guaranteed response / deadline (1); controls a process as it happens (1)', '[{"criterion":"Deadline","marks":1},{"criterion":"Control","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'An OS that responds to sensor inputs within a guaranteed time so it can control the greenhouse as conditions change.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('03ed67c7-b6b5-56ae-89b5-238d0fc776d3', '98a87c80-b4a0-5234-a5fe-4f49fa5c77ce', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): priority pre-emptive scheduling; deterministic; continuous monitoring / feedback; reliable / fault tolerant; small embedded; minimal interface; fast interrupt handling', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Priority-based scheduling. 2 Continuous monitoring of sensors with feedback.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('2c86ecec-2c35-54cd-b1ae-bfa860aa58b6', '72459ba6-a3e7-5dec-95be-0a135f407444', 1, true, 'Fire task higher priority pre-empts logging (1); alarm / sprinklers / heaters off immediately, logging resumes after (1)', '[{"criterion":"Pre-emption","marks":1},{"criterion":"Immediate action","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The fire task has a higher priority, so it interrupts the logging task at once and switches on the alarm and sprinklers; the logging continues afterwards.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('6a759385-533d-5e76-a8c4-b35271dd1fd8', 'c64bb25f-2915-58c3-98cf-1ccf11f8fb14', 1, true, 'Fire-safety hard (1); video soft (1); ABS hard (1)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"✓",""],[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('686f6969-4f5a-53b4-a15a-bfc9c9179fff', '6c398d67-f36e-5d37-b992-d8dff4a228c1', 1, true, 'Any one (1): airbag controller; pacemaker; autopilot; industrial robot; traffic lights; washing machine controller; drone', '[{"criterion":"Valid device","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A car airbag controller.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('9df2ee4f-5a04-50c2-9206-f2a76bc79900', 'd7721b4c-012f-56d4-84ed-635b4504d31a', 1, true, 'NOS provides user authentication and authorization mechanisms… (1) ensuring only authorized users access network resources (1); verifies identities (1) to assign access rights (1) [Max 2]', '[{"criterion":"Authentication","marks":1},{"criterion":"Authorisation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It verifies each user''s name and password at log-in and gives the account the access rights of its group, so only authorised users can use each resource.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('0abd6315-2ec1-5386-8824-8919ddcf7b2e', '6b3cf851-55df-5aa3-a402-4b7c0a161420', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): file sharing; printer sharing / queues; central backup; security / logs; updates; remote administration; DHCP / DNS / e-mail', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Sharing printers. 2 Backing up users'' files centrally.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('26c12e08-dc6d-58b3-a0d9-4be361d0b94a', '86040647-2c4f-52df-90b7-ffc7ce1287cb', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each), both sides: central vs individual control; security; backup; cost; size', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'In the school''s network the server controls all accounts and backups centrally, whereas in peer-to-peer each computer manages its own security and files, which would be impossible to control for 400 computers.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('4d2da603-74cd-55ff-a93f-7ae5bbcb63e0', 'd0b2ba41-a601-5436-bec6-7354b0b87b9d', 1, true, 'Authentication — verifying who the user is (1); authorisation — deciding what the user may access (1)', '[{"criterion":"Authentication","marks":1},{"criterion":"Authorisation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Authentication checks who the user is, for example by password; authorisation then decides which folders and printers that user may use.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('b5694d96-3473-5a96-a2b1-a976c363a6f9', 'e48432ee-c898-576d-b648-2ce20e45da02', 1, true, 'Advantage (1) + explanation (1): automatic / regular — pupils do not need to remember; work can be restored if a PC fails / file deleted', '[{"criterion":"Advantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Backups happen automatically every night, so pupils'' work can be restored even if they forget to save a copy or a computer fails.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('238a9c8c-f832-57ba-9d58-e793fe3a066c', '17bb8ed7-981a-5b32-b96a-e1c6cd5ea0d8', 1, true, 'Jobs with similar requirements are batched together and run as a group (1); data collected for a defined period and processed as a pack (1); sorting before processing (1); no interaction (1) [Max 2]', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Similar jobs are grouped and run together. 2 Data is collected over a period and processed without user interaction.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('ded470fb-7f90-5ad1-8474-b3a710b8a814', '66834a01-07b6-5f08-a4fd-6eecbe70049b', 1, true, 'Any three (1 each): jobs submitted with instructions in advance (JCL / script); placed in a job queue; data sorted (by customer number); run automatically one after another at a scheduled / off-peak time; output spooled to printers / files', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1},{"criterion":"Third","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The billing jobs are submitted with instructions written in advance and placed in a job queue. The meter readings are sorted by customer number, and at night the OS runs the jobs one after another without an operator, spooling the bills to the printers.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('3c635b03-6389-5748-a070-bedbca4f028d', '54552bd2-61cb-5bad-bad8-e273654add64', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): large volume of similar jobs; not urgent / quarterly; readings collected over the period; off-peak automatic', '[{"criterion":"First","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'There are 300 000 similar bills that are only needed once a quarter, so they can all be calculated together automatically at night.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('72fa8d61-6e6e-5790-8dcb-63b6213bb84c', '6a74df92-95cd-5867-a602-22918ae8b8c2', 1, true, 'Disadvantage (1) + explanation (1): error found after the whole batch — all bills reprinted; results delayed; cannot change jobs while running', '[{"criterion":"Disadvantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'If there is an error in the tariff, it may only be noticed after all 300 000 bills are printed, and the whole batch must be run again.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('a84c6a95-fddc-5ea1-a5d8-d3782809c11b', '0653a840-575b-5119-b396-1699a0e43765', 1, true, 'At night / off-peak, when the computer is not busy with other work (1)', '[{"criterion":"Off-peak with reason","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'At night, when the computer is not needed for other work.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
