  ('30726b0c-271d-5a96-9ac6-046b67220da5', '2e551b80-c10b-5ef4-ac59-97be0833ba1c', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): OSI 7 layers vs TCP/IP 4; OSI is a reference / theoretical model vs TCP/IP is used in practice on the Internet; TCP/IP combines application, presentation and session into one application layer; TCP/IP combines data link and physical into network access', '[{"criterion":"Point 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Point 2","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'OSI has seven layers and is a reference model, whereas TCP/IP has four layers and is the model the Internet actually uses; TCP/IP joins OSI''s application, presentation and session layers into one application layer.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('71c6fd6f-fcee-56fa-a7dc-90c33877039e', 'c64316e2-ef4f-56f9-ba6c-dcce17cc32b7', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): each layer developed / changed independently; standards allow equipment from different manufacturers to work together; easier troubleshooting; easier to learn / complex task divided into smaller parts', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Each layer can be changed without affecting the others. 2 Equipment from different manufacturers can work together because it follows the same standards.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
