  ('753ff8d6-2b12-58ee-b6c0-571f9de41dbd', '842e8d15-c7bc-5fe4-b3e3-3c090c80a6ba', 1, true, 'Lexical analysis (max 2): comment and spaces removed (1); lexemes become tokens — price / cost identifiers, = and * operators, 2 number, ; separator; identifiers added to the symbol table (1)
Syntax analysis (max 2): tokens checked against the grammar of an assignment statement (1); parse tree built with * below = / syntax errors reported (1)
Code generation (1): machine instructions produced, e.g. LDA cost, MUL #2, STA price / addresses allocated
Optimisation (1): e.g. multiply by 2 replaced by addition or shift (strength reduction) / redundant instructions removed
[Max 6]', '[{"criterion":"Lexical: comment / spaces removed","marks":1},{"criterion":"Lexical: tokens identified / symbol table","marks":1},{"criterion":"Syntax: checked against grammar","marks":1},{"criterion":"Syntax: parse tree / errors","marks":1},{"criterion":"Code generation described for this statement","marks":1},{"criterion":"Optimisation described for this statement","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'In lexical analysis the comment and spaces are removed and the statement is split into tokens: price (identifier), = (operator), cost (identifier), * (operator), 2 (number) and ; (separator); price and cost are added to the symbol table. In syntax analysis the tokens are checked against the grammar rule for an assignment, and a parse tree is built with cost * 2 under the = node. In code generation machine instructions are produced, for example LDA cost, MUL #2, STA price, using the addresses from the symbol table. In optimisation the multiplication by 2 can be replaced by a faster shift-left or by adding cost to itself.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
