- and tries the next possible fact / rule / value
- This continues until a solution is found or all possibilities have been tried / to find all solutions', '[{"criterion":"Tries facts and rules in order","marks":1},{"criterion":"Goes back to the last choice and tries another option when a match fails","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Prolog tries to match the query with the facts and rules in order. If a sub-goal fails, it goes back to the last point where there was a choice and tries the next fact or rule, until a solution is found or every option has been tried.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('c0a77b29-f18e-5722-bb64-7764692b5d40', 'c9068f90-c0cf-5eae-8029-7e3001faa7e8', 1, true, 'Advantage (1): shorter code; closer to the problem / easier to read; the programmer does not need to write the algorithm; no changing state so fewer side-effect errors; easier to run in parallel; suits databases / AI / expert systems

