  ('a95808d6-d22f-53c5-902f-74a7fe32ab15', 'aadd9fb5-5c36-5843-8622-65edc2878706', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each):
- Declarative focuses on what the program should perform whereas imperative focuses on how to achieve the result
- In declarative programming execution is not clearly delineated whereas an imperative program is a clearly defined sequence of instructions
- Functional, logic and query programming are declarative whereas procedural and object-oriented programming are imperative
- Imperative programs change state (variables) whereas declarative programs have little or no changing state
[Max 2] Accept any correct answer', '[{"criterion":"First valid difference","marks":1},{"criterion":"Second, different valid difference","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 Declarative programming focuses on what the program should achieve, whereas imperative programming focuses on how. 2 An imperative program is a clearly defined sequence of instructions, whereas in declarative programming the order of execution is not clearly delineated.', '{}'::jsonb, 'Do not award the same idea twice.', null),
