  ('259788fa-77f9-50eb-b43a-9bf112280157', 'f8ec5daf-11dc-5115-a03d-d020a99aaa8c', 1, true, 'Advantages (max 3):
- Queries are shorter / quicker to write (1)
- The programmer only describes which records are needed; does not write the search / loops (1)
- The DBMS / query optimiser chooses an efficient way to find the records (1)
- Easier to read / change; fewer logic errors (1)

Disadvantages (max 2):
- Less control over how the records are found (1)
