- AR: reconstruction shown over real ruins / exhibits on phones — visitors see the real artefacts too (1); less immersive (1)
- Justified conclusion (1)
[Max 3]', '[{"criterion":"Valid point about VR","marks":1},{"criterion":"Valid point about AR","marks":1},{"criterion":"Justified conclusion","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'VR would let visitors walk through the whole city as it looked 800 years ago, which is very immersive, but only a few visitors could use the headsets at a time. AR would show the reconstruction on top of the real ruins and artefacts using visitors'' own phones. VR is better here because the city no longer exists, so a complete virtual reconstruction shows it best.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
