  ('69a8d639-6aea-5dc3-9cd3-a83f4db82e3d', '7ab44a82-074d-58cd-9cfd-79389dd11e09', 1, true, 'A program stored on the blockchain that runs automatically when conditions are met (1); example, e.g. payment released when delivery is confirmed / insurance paid when a flight is delayed (1)', '[{"criterion":"Description","marks":1},{"criterion":"Example","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A program on the blockchain that executes automatically when agreed conditions are met, e.g. paying a supplier as soon as delivery is confirmed.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('eb55fe16-9ac7-5580-a8f5-bfac0a16a787', '1b20665e-d645-5774-b66e-04f4a2df7124', 1, true, 'A group controls more than half of the computing power / stake and can rewrite recent blocks / approve its own version (1); on a large network this needs an enormous amount of hardware and electricity, so it is too expensive (1)', '[{"criterion":"Meaning","marks":1},{"criterion":"Why unlikely","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'If one group controlled over half the network''s computing power it could out-mine the honest nodes and rewrite recent blocks; on a network like Bitcoin this would cost far too much.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('999bd4c1-fc41-560a-826c-a29add9b42dc', '7276c1d1-6e76-5703-8735-0e846da56eef', 1, true, 'L1–R1, L2–R2, L3–R3', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3"}}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('b558f259-d0ab-57c8-b0c1-63dd48998c75', '8bb27f1b-6db9-5ef9-abbe-32f2b2c0e2db', 1, true, 'Advantages (1 each, max 2): hard to tamper / data integrity; no central authority / no single point of failure; transparent; fewer intermediaries / lower fees; permanent audit trail. Disadvantages (1 each, max 2): high energy use (PoW); slow; mistakes cannot be undone / lost keys; large storage; legal uncertainty; privacy on public chains.', '[{"criterion":"Advantage 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Advantage 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Disadvantage 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Disadvantage 2","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Advantage 1: records are very hard to tamper with.
Advantage 2: no single point of failure.
Disadvantage 1: proof of work uses a lot of electricity.
Disadvantage 2: lost private keys mean lost assets.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('a7c5d66a-1f19-5445-b0bc-c74443a3f3f8', '49be87cb-0c79-5276-aafe-edccd63d7bce', 1, true, 'Distributed database shared among nodes / list of blocks linked using cryptography / secure decentralised record of transactions (1)', '[{"criterion":"Description","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A decentralised ledger of records grouped into blocks linked by hashes and copied to many nodes.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('2859d10d-cc95-534e-92fe-442aabd7cfc7', 'd4f893e7-a8fa-5818-b3e4-5e68bfaece23', 1, true, 'Any three (1 each): data / transactions (e.g. location of the medicine); timestamp; hash of the block; hash of the previous block; nonce; block number', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1},{"criterion":"3","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '1 The data, e.g. where the batch was delivered
2 A timestamp
3 The hash of the previous block', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('9db2fb54-9e5f-5571-97df-74a7ddfb0655', 'a5a48488-0a52-5069-a284-233d568fccbe', 1, true, 'Changing the record changes the block''s hash (1); it no longer matches the previous hash stored in the next block / every later block would have to be recalculated (1); other nodes hold the original copy, so the majority rejects the change (1)', '[{"criterion":"Hash changes","marks":1},{"criterion":"Link broken","marks":1},{"criterion":"Other copies","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The edited block would get a new hash that does not match the next block''s previous-hash, so the chain breaks; all the other nodes still hold the original chain, so the altered copy is rejected.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('d6a4f352-e4c1-53a4-b08f-4425a82227f0', 'd6b11b29-d03c-5e86-a02e-5cc54e312fda', 1, true, 'Cryptocurrency; smart contracts; financial services; games; domain names; certificates; voting; land registry (1)', '[{"criterion":"Example","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Cryptocurrencies such as Bitcoin.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e785f803-815f-55fd-ad6b-d98d4dcc5457', '676cdb55-15e2-535d-aefc-99c983d3b7ac', 1, true, 'Any four (1 each): Dana signs the transaction with her private key; it is broadcast to the network of nodes; nodes validate it (signature / enough balance); it is grouped with others into a block; nodes reach consensus / a miner solves the proof of work; the block is added to every copy of the chain', '[{"criterion":"Step 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Step 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Step 3","marks":1},{"criterion":"Step 4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Dana signs the transaction with her private key and it is broadcast to the nodes. The nodes validate the signature and her balance, then put it in a block with other transactions. A miner solves the proof of work and the block is added to every copy of the chain.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('7c4db35c-dc1d-5999-8e83-27045c3e8d1b', '6265ba68-dc72-5ec0-8fb0-129a40c36ff0', 1, true, 'Private: secret, used to sign / authorise the transaction, proving it is from Dana (1); public: shared, used by nodes to verify the signature / as her address (1)', '[{"criterion":"Private","marks":1},{"criterion":"Public","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Private key: kept secret; Dana signs the transaction with it.
Public key: nodes use it to check that the signature is Dana''s.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('4bc081b1-8407-596a-b8c8-e68e989adfa3', '04b58f3f-9971-56aa-bdc0-34c56b4e2f24', 1, true, 'Blockchain: copied to many nodes / decentralised, no single owner (1); bank: one organisation controls and can edit the records / single point of failure / users must trust the bank (1)', '[{"criterion":"Blockchain","marks":1},{"criterion":"Bank","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'On a blockchain every node has a copy and no one controls it, while a bank''s database is held and controlled by one organisation that users must trust.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('de8f7c09-dddc-5f86-97cd-cc4354026540', '80d3c4df-2203-501b-81e9-23ed6dcd788d', 1, true, 'Miners compete to solve a puzzle (1); repeatedly change the nonce and calculate the hash until it meets the target, e.g. starts with zeros (1); the first miner broadcasts the block, others check it easily and add it; the miner is rewarded (1)', '[{"criterion":"Competition","marks":1},{"criterion":"Nonce / hash target","marks":1},{"criterion":"Broadcast, verify, reward","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Miners compete: each changes the nonce and recalculates the block''s hash until it starts with the required zeros. The first to succeed broadcasts the block; other nodes quickly verify it and add it, and the miner gets a reward.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('4a860f11-902c-540a-a2a6-adfe6b65ba6d', '5e8f432c-6efe-5a0e-9d25-1412c500cd1d', 1, true, 'PoW uses huge amounts of electricity (1); PoS chooses validators by the coins they stake, so no energy-intensive puzzle is needed (1)', '[{"criterion":"Disadvantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"PoS","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Proof of work uses a lot of electricity; proof of stake picks validators by their staked coins, so no puzzle has to be solved.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('c63cf638-3f51-5092-b187-10a4c63bcdda', '7969dcc5-9d4d-558b-8c5a-3f72662b854d', 1, true, 'Fixed length / deterministic / one-way / small change gives a completely different hash / collision-resistant (1)', '[{"criterion":"Property","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'A small change in the data gives a completely different hash.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('7d621fae-b8e7-583d-ab75-ed68874d8491', '6ef3b021-d410-5254-b5eb-c321498f5817', 1, true, 'Advantage: employers can verify diplomas / they cannot be forged or changed (1); disadvantage: mistakes cannot be easily corrected / personal data visible / cost, energy, storage / lost keys (1)', '[{"criterion":"Advantage","marks":1},{"criterion":"Disadvantage","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Advantage: employers can check a diploma is genuine because it cannot be forged.
