  ('ee47043e-93a7-5314-b3d9-dc918825157f', '27781f22-be57-58ce-aa7a-66dd3fbbcdd1', 1, true, 'Any four (1 each): CPU sends part of the document to the printer buffer; CPU returns to other tasks; printer prints from the buffer at its own speed; when the buffer is empty the printer sends an interrupt; CPU saves its task / refills the buffer and returns; repeats until the document is printed', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1},{"criterion":"3","marks":1},{"criterion":"4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The CPU fills the printer buffer with part of the document and goes back to other tasks. The printer prints from the buffer at its own speed. When the buffer is empty it sends an interrupt; the CPU pauses its task, refills the buffer and carries on. This repeats until the whole document is printed.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('afb49e11-d8c1-5dca-99da-fd2e9b202530', '656d4940-0322-587d-8ab1-e54e9c3b06d0', 1, true, 'B', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"B"}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('ef9c5460-fa15-5557-a772-f65a83ca6095', 'd8b64711-99f3-57d3-80d9-8dcecd73bb0e', 1, true, 'ALU: processes and manipulates data; carries out arithmetic (+, −, ×, ÷) and logic (AND, OR, NOT) operations (1). CU: manages the execution of instructions; directs the processor; tells memory, ALU and I/O devices how to respond (1). Accept any reasonable answer.', '[{"criterion":"ALU","marks":1},{"criterion":"CU","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'ALU: carries out arithmetic and logic operations on data.
CU: manages the execution of instructions and sends control signals to memory, the ALU and I/O devices.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('83bb1299-3d18-5911-a42f-62fc4592b23f', 'f8be7238-ce95-5255-9a22-1bf01a1920b1', 1, true, 'L1–R1 … L5–R5.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"pairs":{"L1":"R1","L2":"R2","L3":"R3","L4":"R4","L5":"R5"}}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('2939560b-7373-59c4-ba0f-2b7eb9db851e', '31bfcf95-6c29-5742-9e13-adaf081a5f11', 1, true, 'Any four (1 each): address in PC copied to MAR; MAR places address on the address bus; CU sends memory read signal on the control bus; instruction returns on the data bus into the MDR; instruction copied to the CIR; PC incremented', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1},{"criterion":"3","marks":1},{"criterion":"4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The address in the PC is copied to the MAR and put on the address bus. The control unit sends a memory-read signal on the control bus. The instruction comes back on the data bus into the MDR, is copied into the CIR, and the PC is incremented.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e3bcf31e-bf03-5065-8df1-c7f43ed56251', '5640847d-cc52-52ad-956c-d98a192c1c9f', 1, true, 'Control; data; address (1 each)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"","","✓"],[null,"","✓",""],[null,"✓","",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('056c2914-f905-5379-8795-7d1e31f9ee6d', '70b728a5-effc-5588-9043-c79f4f7822c2', 1, true, '- Instructions and data share the same memory / bus (1)
- only one can be transferred at a time, so the CPU waits for memory / throughput limited (1)
- reduced by cache / pipelining / multiple cores / wider buses / Harvard-style separate caches (1)', '[{"criterion":"Shared path","marks":1},{"criterion":"CPU waits","marks":1},{"criterion":"Solution","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Instructions and data use the same path between the CPU and memory, so they cannot be transferred at the same time and the CPU often waits for memory. Cache memory reduces this by keeping frequently used data close to the CPU.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('9a873fca-edbc-5062-84af-c7c9a1100853', '9d727784-dea5-5921-abd1-e69fbdbc3042', 1, true, 'False.', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":false}'::jsonb, null, 'Cache, number of cores, architecture and memory latency also affect performance.'),
  ('977fbf25-9e07-5e0b-b0e6-ffab0f4108ab', '811173e5-9d2b-5bd6-bbf6-10567fea09e9', 1, true, 'Computer memory that loses its contents when the power is turned off (1)', '[{"criterion":"Loses contents without power","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Memory that loses its contents when the power is turned off.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
