  ('4d7a6032-4ff1-5357-ae7c-70221358d7b1', '9375e5e4-edd9-5c2a-913b-77fc6fdc21ff', 1, true, '- RAM is volatile / empty when the computer is switched on (1)
- ROM keeps the boot program (BIOS/UEFI) that tests the hardware and loads the OS into RAM (1)', '[{"criterion":"RAM empty at start","marks":1},{"criterion":"Boot program in ROM","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'When the computer is switched on RAM is empty, so the boot program stored in non-volatile ROM is needed to start the computer and load the operating system into RAM.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('9c65305d-e0b7-5f18-ba2e-c2493f074ea1', '10cfb6c7-1d6a-50d9-8964-21a48e9e177e', 1, true, 'ROM: stores the control program / washing programmes (1) which must not change and must be kept when the power is off (1). RAM: stores the user''s input (1), e.g. the chosen spin speed / washing programme / temperature / time left / sensor readings, which change each wash (1)', '[{"criterion":"ROM content","marks":1},{"criterion":"ROM reason","marks":1},{"criterion":"RAM content","marks":1},{"criterion":"RAM example","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'ROM: holds the control program for all the washing programmes, which never changes and is kept without power. RAM: stores the user''s choices such as the spin speed and temperature, and the time remaining, which change for every wash.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('69aea5da-ec00-55a7-9d04-c41b97a380a3', 'a84a7e2c-bb31-5d8c-b6cf-cf7583282838', 1, true, 'SRAM; DRAM; DRAM (1 each)', '[{"criterion":"Row 1","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 2","marks":1},{"criterion":"Row 3","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"","✓"],[null,"✓",""],[null,"✓",""]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('21800d79-c678-5d0f-ac3c-73edb269026b', '1620d2be-1660-5b92-8176-21507b7e6ffd', 1, true, 'Any two (1 each): frees up space in RAM; increases the memory available beyond the physical RAM; allows more programs / multiple tasks to run at once; allows larger programs to run', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'It frees up space in RAM by moving unused data to the disk, so more memory is available than the physical RAM and more programs can run at once.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('b4bc2b1d-d3a5-54ff-b551-ae720311e03e', '6c27d8d2-b0d7-51ff-bfeb-322b87a49ade', 1, true, 'Increase RAM / increase virtual memory (page file) / reduce application cache sizes / close some programs (1)', '[{"criterion":"One way","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Install more RAM.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('11e23b55-51a5-5e86-81e2-2214608ed903', '5d6b850d-aa14-5382-ad3c-67c58efa87d9', 1, true, '- The computer spends more time moving pages between RAM and disk than running programs (1)
- happens when RAM is too small for the programs open, so virtual memory is used constantly (1)
- fix: add more RAM / close programs (1)', '[{"criterion":"Definition","marks":1},{"criterion":"Cause","marks":1},{"criterion":"Fix","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Disk thrashing is when the computer keeps swapping pages between RAM and the disk and has little time left to run programs. It happens because RAM is too small for the open programs. Adding RAM or closing programs stops it.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('117c0ee2-8879-5e60-91ec-a4ec3f55d7f5', 'e085d678-1305-57ff-8780-a13a0b03de45', 1, true, '(1) pages (2) page file (3) RAM', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"blanks":[["pages"],["page file","swap file","pagefile"],["RAM","main memory"]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('2f37ef59-b326-534e-b30f-6f386fd3bc00', '43025072-4063-5273-a89e-9d5731cd61b4', 1, true, 'Cache is located closer to / in the CPU (1) which reduces the time to access data (1); OR cache is much smaller so data is found faster (1)(1); OR cache uses SRAM (1) with lower latency / no refresh (1)', '[{"criterion":"Reason","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Cache is built into (or next to) the CPU, so the data travels a much shorter distance and is reached in less time.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('07329d02-7340-533d-97df-ec7119b3ca1a', 'a886304b-e0fe-53c0-8fd7-5fcfcf6b5b4b', 1, true, 'Hit: the data the CPU needs is found in the cache and used immediately (1). Miss: the data is not in the cache and must be fetched from RAM (then copied into the cache) (1)', '[{"criterion":"Hit","marks":1},{"criterion":"Miss","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Cache hit: the required data is already in the cache. Cache miss: it is not, so it must be fetched from the slower RAM.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('7d9103d1-e165-544e-a762-d56a289b87f4', '26ca1985-9c3b-5e1e-90be-a474dd979076', 1, true, 'B', '[]'::jsonb, null, '{"correct":"B"}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('e68eba58-40ef-5b48-8f29-4fc374dfb33f', 'fc23f5ef-6219-5430-bf23-2cf45143353d', 1, true, 'More data / instructions can be held in the cache → more cache hits (1); fewer slow accesses to RAM, so the CPU waits less and performance improves (1)', '[{"criterion":"More hits","marks":1},{"criterion":"Fewer RAM accesses","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'More instructions and data fit in the cache, so there are more cache hits and fewer slow trips to RAM, making the CPU faster.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('a2c71ba9-a4af-500c-b2f4-683438949cdc', '78d22aae-0fd9-53cb-8c8e-05658af2b120', 1, true, 'Registers; cache; RAM; HDD (1 each)', '[{"criterion":"1","marks":1},{"criterion":"2","marks":1},{"criterion":"3","marks":1},{"criterion":"4","marks":1}]'::jsonb, null, '{"rows":[[null,"registers||register"],[null,"cache"],[null,"RAM||main memory"],[null,"HDD||hard disk"]]}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('0c805d2b-7adb-5b5e-b8ef-d36c19580c8d', '9f5be2aa-ed6c-5486-b92a-c7ee828c8add', 1, true, 'RAM is full so virtual memory on the SSD is used (1); moving pages between RAM and disk is slow / thrashing (1)', '[{"criterion":"RAM full / VM","marks":1},{"criterion":"Slow swapping","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'The 8 GB of RAM is full, so the OS moves pages to virtual memory on the SSD; swapping them back and forth is much slower than RAM, so the game freezes.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('3f7d6c9a-2341-5352-aa89-2fada276f415', 'cb7c643c-9793-55f1-a65d-7b65ecd94faa', 1, true, 'More RAM (1); more programs and data fit in RAM so less virtual memory / swapping is needed (1)', '[{"criterion":"More RAM","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Upgrade to 16 GB of RAM, so all the programs fit in main memory and the computer no longer needs to swap to the SSD.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
