• If block (check discount) (1)
• Loop back to the start (1)
• Correct declaration of fee (15000, 18000) (1)
• Correct calculation (annual fee) (1)
• Correct calculation (fee with discount) (1)
[8]
Accept other correct flowchart. Do not award marks for wrong shapes of the elements.', '[{"criterion":"Inputs grade, groupNum","marks":1},{"criterion":"Output fee / error message","marks":1},{"criterion":"Decisions checking the grade","marks":1},{"criterion":"Decision checking the discount","marks":1},{"criterion":"Loop back to the input for an invalid grade","marks":1},{"criterion":"fee = 15000 / 18000","marks":1},{"criterion":"Annual fee = fee × 12","marks":1},{"criterion":"Discount fee = fee × 0.9","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'START → INPUT grade, groupNum → IF grade >= 7 AND grade <= 9 THEN fee = 15000, ELSE IF grade >= 10 AND grade <= 12 THEN fee = 18000, ELSE OUTPUT "ERROR" and loop back to the input → fee = fee × 12 → IF groupNum > 6 THEN fee = fee × 0.9 → OUTPUT fee → END', '{}'::jsonb, 'Accept other correct flowcharts. Do not award marks for elements drawn with the wrong shapes (decision = diamond, input/output = parallelogram, process = rectangle).', null),
  ('46c6bec2-d73e-593d-a656-3eee1be6a3aa', '45643f6c-a79e-54f6-8aac-dc051cb18e9c', 1, true, 'Level 1 DFD elements:
• Entity(s) (manager is required) (1)
• Processes (calculate tuition fee, apply discount) (2)
• Data store (1)
• Defined data flow (1)
[5]
Example: manager —grade, number of students→ Calculate fee —value of fee→ D Results of fee —value of fee→ Output fee —value of fee→ manager.

Accept other correct notations of DFD and correct solutions; accept other correct entities, data stores and processes which satisfy the scenario and logic.
Do not award marks for wrong shapes, or for violation of the rules:
1. Entity can''t be related directly to another entity
2. Entity can''t be related directly to data store
3. Data store can''t be related directly to another data store
4. All data flows must be labelled
5. Data flows can''t be bidirectional
6. All processes and storages should have both incoming and outgoing data flows
7. All data flows must have directions', '[{"criterion":"Entity (manager)","marks":1},{"criterion":"Process: calculate tuition fee","marks":1},{"criterion":"Process: apply discount / output fee","marks":1},{"criterion":"Data store","marks":1},{"criterion":"Labelled, directed data flows","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Manager —grade, number of students→ (1 Calculate fee) —value of fee→ [D1 Results of fee] —value of fee→ (2 Output fee) —value of fee→ Manager', '{}'::jsonb, 'Do not award marks for wrong shapes or violations of DFD rules (entity–entity, entity–store, store–store, unlabelled, bidirectional or undirected flows, processes/stores without both input and output).', null),
