  ('012deed5-6fbd-5b20-b0f4-cc9fba9eaf67', '0b9130a0-a861-5d3f-8e2b-a98c26d79daa', 1, true, 'Calculate Lp and term with power operator instead of a loop (1) To reduce number of iterations (1)
Replace loop Lp=Lp*L with Lp=L^K (1) This reduces K repeated multiplications to one operation (1)
Replace loop term=term*e with term=e^L (1) This reduces L repeated multiplications to one operation (1)
[Max: 2] 1 mark for the method of optimisation; 1 mark for explaining how efficiency is improved. Accept valid alternative answers.', '[{"criterion":"Method","marks":1},{"criterion":"How efficiency improves","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Replace the loop Lp = Lp * L with Lp = L^K; this replaces K repeated multiplications with one operation.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('b92769b3-33d4-5450-8b1e-668a8c22ac87', '3a93ba55-d5ce-5083-9e43-b9def05e183d', 1, true, 'Use L^K directly in the Poisson formula instead of storing it in Lp / Perform the calculation in the output statement instead of using variable Poisson (1)
This removes unnecessary intermediate variables (1)
[2] 1 mark for the method of optimisation; 1 mark for explaining how efficiency is improved. Accept valid alternative answers.', '[{"criterion":"Method","marks":1},{"criterion":"Explanation","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Calculate L^K directly inside the Poisson formula instead of storing it in Lp; this removes an unnecessary intermediate variable, so less memory is used.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null),
  ('b14901a8-ab99-59e4-a3bc-5ca77934e4eb', '6258befe-e168-5de9-a47e-189e8384ae1b', 1, true, 'Use clear and meaningful variable names (1)
Replace generic names like Lp, Ep, and term with descriptive ones like lambdaPowerK and exponentialNegativeLambda (1)
Write comments to explain the code / help other developers understand its purpose and logic (1)
Use white space to make the code easy to read (1)
Use indentation to show the structure of the code (1)
Use error handling to prevent crashes and unexpected behaviour (1)
[Max: 1] Accept valid alternative answers.', '[{"criterion":"Good practice","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Use meaningful variable names, e.g. lambdaPowerK instead of Lp.', '{}'::jsonb, null, null)
on conflict do nothing;

